hadiths[605]{hadithnumber,text}:
"9681","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ikrima, he said: Safiyya, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), sold a house of hers to Mu'awiya for a hundred thousand, and said to a Jewish relative of hers, and said to him: become Muslim, for if you become Muslim you will inherit me. He refused, so she bequeathed to him. Some said: thirty thousand."
"9682","From al-Thawri, from Layth, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: Safiyya bint Huyayy bequeathed to a Jewish nephew of hers."
"9683","Al-Thawri reported from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, he said: the bequest of a Muslim to a Christian is allowed. Al-Thawri said: his bequest to people at war is not allowed."
"9684","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: what is His saying: except that you do kindness to your allies? He said: giving. I said to him: the giving of a believer to a disbeliever with kinship between them? He said: yes, his giving to him in life and his bequest to him."
"9685","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: a Muslim may bequeath to a disbeliever. Ma'mar said: al-Hasan and Qatada said it."
"9686","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, about His saying: except that you do kindness to your allies. He said: except that you have a relative not upon your religion, so you bequeath him something; he is your ally in lineage, not your ally in religion. He said: and al-Hasan said the same."
"9687","Ibn Jurayj reported: Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Alqama reported to me, from Ibn Abi Husayn: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a Jewish neighbor of good character. He fell ill, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited him with his Companions and said: do you testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? He looked at his father; his father was silent and the boy was silent. Then a second time, then a third. His father said at the third: say what he said to you. So he did, then died. The Jews wanted to take charge of him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: we are more entitled to him than you. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed him, shrouded him, embalmed him, and prayed over him. Abd al-Razzaq said: I heard it from Abdullah ibn Amr."
"9688","My father reported to me, from Ikrima client of Ibn Abbas, he said: a Muslim visits a disbeliever and says: how are you in the morning? How are you in the evening? When he leaves, he says: O Allah, destroy him, relieve the Muslims of him, and spare them his burden."
"9689","From Ibn Jurayj, Ata said: if there is close kinship between a Muslim and a disbeliever, let the Muslim visit the disbeliever. Amr ibn Dinar said it as opinion."
"9690","From Ma'mar, from Qatada: except that you fear from them a fear. He said: except that there is kinship between him and him, so he maintains ties for that."
"9691","Ibn Jurayj reported: I heard Sulayman ibn Musa saying: we visit Christian tribes though there is no kinship between us and them."
"9692","Al-Thawri reported from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Talib fell ill, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came visiting him."
"9693","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ata said to me: if there is close kinship between a Muslim and a disbeliever, he follows his funeral. Amr said it as opinion."
"9694","Al-Thawri reported from Hammad, from al-Sha'bi, he said: the mother of al-Harith ibn Abi Rabi'a died, and she was Christian, so the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) escorted her. Al-Thawri said in part of the hadith: he was ordered to walk in front of her."
"9695","Husayn ibn Mihran reported from Layth, from Abdullah ibn Sharik, he said: a man asked Ibn Umar, saying: my mother died while Christian, shall I attend her burial? Ibn Umar said to him: walk in front of her, for you are not with her."
"9696","Ma'mar reported from Qatada, he said: a Muslim follows the funeral of his disbelieving father, walking alongside it, not near it."
"9697","Muhammad ibn Rashid reported: the mother of Khalid ibn Abdillah al-Qasri died, and she was Christian, so he called the bishops of Christians in Damascus and said: do with her what you do with daughters of your kings, for she is of kings daughters. He said: he ordered his wives, and they were the ones who took charge of her, and they taught them. He said: when they finished and she was carried, he rode, and notables rode with him, and walked alongside her. When he reached the grave with her, he turned his mount away and said: this is the last of our kindness to the mother of Jarir. Then he said: I did with her only what Abdullah ibn Abi Zakariya did with his mother. Muhammad said: Abdullah ibn Abi Zakariya was of the worshippers of Syria, its jurists and its elite; Makhul used to learn from him."
"9698","Muhammad ibn Rashid reported: I heard Makhul saying: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) followed the funeral of Abu Talib walking alongside it, and did not pray over him, saying: kinship kept you joined, and may you be rewarded good. He said: and he did not stand over his grave."
"9699","Ma'mar reported from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Sulayman ibn Musa saying: do not follow their funerals, though there is kinship between you and them."
"9700","From Ibn Jurayj, Hisham ibn Urwa reported to me, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: my mother came while polytheist in the treaty of Quraysh when they treated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and their term with her father. So I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has come while desiring, shall I maintain ties with her? He said: yes, maintain ties with your mother."
"9701","From Ma'mar, he said: it reached me that al-Harith ibn Abi Rabi'a did not follow the funeral of his mother, and the mother of al-Harith was disbelieving."
"9702","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ata said to me: he neither washes him nor shrouds him, meaning the disbeliever, though there is close kinship between them."
"9703","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ismail ibn Muslim reported to me, from Abu Ishaq, he said: Ali came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: this stray old man, Abu Talib, has died. He said: wash him, then wash as you wash from major impurity, then conceal him. He said: I would not do it. He said: order another."
"9704","Ma'mar and al-Thawri reported from Najiya ibn Ka'b al-Asadi that when Abu Talib died, Ali went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, your stray old uncle has died, who will bury him? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: go bury your father, and when you finish do not do anything until you come to me. He said: so I came to him, and he ordered me and I washed, then he supplicated for me with supplications than which nothing on earth would please me more."
"9705","Ibn Uyayna reported from Abu Sinan, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: the father of a man died while Jewish, and his son did not follow him. That was mentioned to Ibn Abbas, and Ibn Abbas said: what was upon him if he washed him, followed him, and sought forgiveness for him while alive, meaning: supplicated for him while the father was alive. He said: then Ibn Abbas recited: when it became clear to him that he was an enemy of Allah, he dissociated from him, meaning: when he died upon his disbelief."
"9706","Ibn Uyayna reported from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he was placed in his pit. He met him and ordered him, so he was taken out, and he placed him on his knees, dressed him in his shirt, and blew upon him of his saliva, Allah knows best. Al-Thawri said: when non-Arabs die young with a Muslim, he prays over them; if he did not take them out of their lands, he prays over them when they fall into his hands. Al-Thawri said: and Hammad said: when he owns the young, he is Muslim."
"9707","Al-Thawri reported from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal ibn Abd al-Muttalib, that Abbas said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): what have you availed your uncle Abu Talib? He used to protect you and anger for you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: he is in a shallow part of Fire, and were it not for me he would be in the lowest depth of Fire."
"9708","Ma'mar reported: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote about slaves of dhimmis who become Muslim that they be sold."
"9709","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ata said to me: a Muslim does not carry the bier of a disbeliever."
"9710","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ata said to me: nor stands over his grave, though there is kinship between them."
"9711","From Ma'mar, he said: if a Jew or Christian were with me and died, with none of his religion with him, I would bury him, and not leave beasts to eat him, nor wash him, nor pray over him."
"9712","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ata said to me: let the disbeliever follow the funeral of a Muslim. And Amr likewise."
"9713","Ibn Jurayj reported: I heard Sulayman ibn Musa saying: they used to follow our funerals."
"9714","Abd al-Razzaq said: Sulayman ibn Dawud died, and Jews and Christians followed him with the Muslims. Ma'mar said: there is no harm in it."
"9715","I heard Ibn Jurayj and al-Thawri saying: a Muslim consoles a dhimmi, saying: to Allah belongs authority and greatness; live, O son of Adam, as you live, but death is inevitable."
"9716","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said to me: let the disbeliever stand at the grave of the Muslim if he wishes"
"9717","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said to me: let the disbeliever stand (at the grave) even if there is no kinship between the two"
"9718","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata said to me: a disbeliever may not wash the Muslim. From Hisham, from al-Hasan, the same"
"9719","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata said to me: a disbeliever may not carry the bier of the Muslim. And Amr ibn Dinar said: he may carry his bier"
"9720","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I said to Ata: may the Muslim slave be sold to the disbeliever? He said: No, as an opinion. Ibn Jurayj said: and Amr ibn Dinar said to me: No, as an opinion"
"9721","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Sulayman ibn Musa saying: a disbeliever may not enslave a Muslim"
"9722","Mamar and al-Thawri informed us, from Amr ibn Maymun, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote concerning the slaves of the dhimmis who become Muslim, ordering that they be sold. Al-Thawri said: and likewise we say, they are sold"
"9723","Al-Hasan ibn Umarah informed us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Ibrahim, he said: when a Christian slave becomes Muslim, (his master) is compelled to sell him"
"9724","Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, he said: Hakim ibn Zurayq informed me that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote to his father: To proceed, I have written to our officials not to leave a Muslim slave with a Christian except that he is seized and sold, nor a Muslim woman under a Christian except that they separate them; so carry that out in your district"
"9725","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab was asked about a Christian man under whom was a Christian slave-girl of his who bore him a child, then she became Muslim. He said: Islam separates between them, and she and her child are freed. Ibn Jurayj said: and I say: she is not freed until her master is called to Islam; if he refuses to become Muslim she is freed, and if he becomes Muslim she remains his slave-girl"
"9726","From al-Thawri, concerning a Christian umm walad who became Muslim, he said: her own value is assessed against her and she works to pay off her price, and she is separated from him; if he dies she is freed, and if he becomes Muslim after her working, she is sold and does not return to him; and if he dies whether Muslim or Christian, there is no labor-due upon her. Al-Thawri said concerning a Christian mudabbar the same as he said concerning his umm walad. Al-Thawri said concerning a dhimmi with whom a slave becomes Muslim and he hides him or conceals him, he said: he is disciplined and (the slave) is sold"
"9727","Ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote: do not buy any real estate of the dhimmis nor anything of their lands"
"9728","Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, he said: Harmalah ibn Imran informed me that Ali ibn Talq informed him that a Christian umm walad from Palestine became Muslim, so he wrote about her to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, and Umar wrote to him: send men to assess her value, and when her value is fixed pay it to him from the treasury, for she is a woman of the Muslims"
"9729","From Mamar, from Amr ibn Maymun ibn Mihran, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote concerning whoever becomes Muslim of the slaves of the dhimmis that they be sold, and that the dhimmis not be left to enslave them, and that their prices be paid to their owners; and whoever after your order to him is found having enslaved any of the Muslim captives who has become Muslim and prays, then free him"
"9730","From al-Thawri, and he was asked about the non-Arab slaves who come out of the sea and elsewhere, may they be sold to the Jews and Christians? He said: if they are adults Islam is presented to them; if they become Muslim (so be it), otherwise they are sold to the Jews and Christians if their owner wishes. What is recommended in that is that when a Muslim owns Jews by purchase or captivity, he calls them to Islam; if they refuse except to hold to their religion, the Muslim may if he wishes sell them to the dhimmis, but he may not sell them to anyone of the people at war. And if they are upon other than a (recognized) religion, like the Indian and the Zanj, the Muslim may not sell them to anyone, neither of the dhimmis nor of the people at war, and may sell them only to the Muslims, because they respond when called and have no religion they hold to, and the Jews and Christians should not be allowed to Judaize them or Christianize them. And if the non-Arabs are children, they may not be sold to the Jews and Christians; they are sold only to the Muslims"
"9731","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, he said: when the Muslim owns them as children, that is their Islam"
"9732","From al-Thawri, and he was asked about Muslim merchants who enter the lands of the non-Arabs, where some of them enslave others, is it right for him to buy them while he knows? He said: Yes"
"9733","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from a man of Banu Ghifar, he said: Umar said: do not buy the slaves of the dhimmis, for they are people of kharaj, some of them pay on behalf of others from their home-born (slaves). Abd al-Razzaq said: their tilad is what is born among them"
"9734","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab said concerning a man of the People of the Book who secretly bought a Muslim slave-girl and she bore him a child, he said: he is punished and she is taken from him"
"9735","Mamar informed us, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote concerning whoever becomes Muslim of the slaves of the dhimmis that they be sold"
"9736","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: a trustworthy person informed me that a Christian freed a Muslim, so Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said: give him his price from the treasury, and his wala is for the Muslims"
"9737","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I was told a report raised to Ali ibn Abi Talib concerning a Jew or Christian who becomes a heretic, he said: leave him to move from one religion to another"
"9738","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Khalad informed me that Amr ibn Shuayb informed him that Umar ibn al-Khattab would not leave a Jew or Christian to Christianize his child nor to Judaize him in the dominion of the Arabs"
"9739","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, he said: I heard Bajalah al-Tamimi saying: I was a scribe for Jaz ibn Muawiyah, uncle of al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, when the letter of Umar came a year before his death: kill every sorcerer, separate every mahram couple among the Magians, and forbid them the zamzamah (humming). He said: so we killed three sorceresses. He said: and Jaz prepared much food and invited the Magians, and they threw down the crutches they used to eat with, about a mule-load or two mule-loads of silver, and ate without humming. He said: and Umar had not taken the jizyah from the Magians until Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf testified that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it from the Magians of Hajar"
"9740","Ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Bajalah al-Tamimi narrating to Abu al-Shatha and Amr ibn Aws at the portico of Zamzam during the governorship of Musab ibn al-Zubayr, then he mentioned the like of the report of Ibn Jurayj"
"9741","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Kurdus al-Taghlibi, he said: a man of Taghlib came to Umar, and Umar said to him: you had a share in the pre-Islamic age, so take your share of Islam. So he made peace with him on doubling the jizyah upon them and that they not Christianize children"
"9742","Ibn al-Taymi informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Saib, from al-Asbagh ibn Nubatah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he made peace with the Christians of Banu Taghlib on condition that they not Christianize children; if they do, they have no covenant. He said: and Ali said: if I were free I would fight them"
"9743","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from more than one, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote to Adi ibn Artah asking al-Hasan: why were the Magians left to marry mothers and sisters? So he asked him, and he said: the polytheism they are upon is greater than that, and they were left to it only for the sake of the jizyah"
"9744","Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, he said: Umar would not leave a Christian, Jew or Magian entering Madinah to stay in it except three (days), enough to sell their goods. When Umar was struck, he said: I had commanded you that none of them enter upon us; had the afflicted one been other than me he would have had a decision in it. He said: and it was said: two religions do not coexist in it"
"9745","From Mamar, from Ayyub, he said: when Umar was stabbed, he sent for the people of the Emigrants, among them Ali, and said: was this with your consent? Ali said: Allah forbid that it be with our consent; had we been able to add from our lifespans to your life we would have done so. He said: I had forbidden you that any of them enter upon us"
"9746","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: the Jews, Christians and other disbelievers who came to Madinah as travelers would not remain more than three days in the time of Umar; I do not know whether that was done with them before that or not"
"9747","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata said to me: no polytheist may enter the whole Haram, and he recited: after this year of theirs"
"9748","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata and Amr ibn Dinar said to me: His saying, so let them not approach the Sacred Mosque after this year of theirs, means the whole Haram"
"9749","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed us that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying concerning this verse, the polytheists are but impure so let them not approach the Sacred Mosque: except that he be a slave or one of the people of the jizyah"
"9750","Mamar informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, he said: I lived at a time when no Jew or Christian was left to enter the Haram, and they would not tread it except stealthily"
"9751","Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: two religions do not coexist in the land of the Arabs, or he said: in the land of the Hijaz. He said: so Umar investigated that until he found confirmation of it. Al-Zuhri said: for that reason Umar expelled them. Al-Zuhri said: and Umar would not leave the dhimmis to stay in Madinah more than three days when they wanted to sell food, and the Jewish and Christian women were ordered to veil and adorn themselves"
"9752","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I shall surely expel the Jews and Christians from the Arabian Peninsula until I leave in it none but a Muslim"
"9753","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I was told from Ali ibn Husayn that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expelled the Jews from Madinah. Muslim ibn Abi Maryam narrates it from him"
"9754","Malik informed us, from Ismail ibn Abi Hakim, that he heard Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz saying: the last words the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke were: May Allah curse the Jews and Christians, they took the graves of their prophets as mosques; there shall not remain, or two religions shall not coexist, in the land of the Arabs"
"9755","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Jews of Banu al-Nadir and Qurayzah fought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expelled Banu al-Nadir and left Qurayzah and those under them until Qurayzah fought after that; then he killed their men and divided their women, children and properties among the Muslims, except some of them who joined the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he granted them safety and they became Muslim. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expelled all the Jews of Madinah: Banu Qaynuqa, who are the people of Abdillah ibn Salam, and the Jews of Banu Harithah, and every Jew in Madinah"
"9756","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab expelled the Jews and Christians from the land of the Hijaz. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prevailed over Khaybar, wanted to expel the Jews from it, so the Jews asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to leave them in it on condition they do its work for him, with half the fruit for them. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: we leave you in it upon that as long as we wish. So they remained in it until Umar expelled them to Tayma and Ariha"
"9757","Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed Khaybar to the Jews to work in it, with half its fruit for them. That continued in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and the early part of Umar's caliphate. Then Umar was told that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the illness in which he died: two religions do not coexist in the land of the Arabs, or he said: in the land of the Hijaz. So he investigated that until he found confirmation of it, then he called them and said: whoever has a covenant from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), let him bring it, otherwise I shall expel you. He said: so Umar expelled them"
"9758","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab heard a Jewish man saying: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: as if I see you having put your saddle on your camel, then traveling night after night. So Umar said: by Allah, you shall not walk about with it. The Jew said: by Allah, I never saw a word harder upon the one who said it and lighter upon the one to whom it was said than it"
"9759","Ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn Abbas said to me: Thursday, and what is Thursday? Then he wept until his tears soaked the pebbles. I said: O Abu Abbas, and what is Thursday? He said: the day the pain of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intensified. He said: bring me, I shall write for you a document after which you will never go astray. He said: so they disputed, and dispute is not fitting in the presence of a prophet. They said: what is wrong with him, delirium? Ask him to explain. He said: leave me, for what I am in is better than what you call me to. He said: and at his death he enjoined three things, saying: expel the polytheists from the Arabian Peninsula, and honor the delegations as I used to honor them. He said: either Said deliberately fell silent about the third, or he said it and I forgot it"
"9760","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: it reached me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined at his death that no Jew or Christian be left in the land of the Hijaz, that the army of Usamah be sent forth to Syria, and he enjoined good treatment of the Copts, for they have kinship"
"9761","Al-Hasan ibn Umarah informed us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Zabyan, he said: I heard Ali saying: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: if you are given authority after me, expel the people of Najran from the Arabian Peninsula"
"9762","Ibn al-Taymi informed us, from Layth, from Tawus, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: the Jews and Christians may not share your towns with you except by becoming Muslim; whoever of them apostatizes and refuses, nothing is accepted from him short of his blood"
"9763","Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Kab ibn Malik, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: when you gain possession of the Copts, treat them well, for they have a covenant of protection and kinship. Mamar said: so I said to al-Zuhri: meaning the mother of Ibrahim, son of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: rather the mother of Ismail. Ibn Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Kab ibn Malik, the same. Al-Thawri informed us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from al-Zuhri, the same, his saying: they have kinship. Abd al-Razzaq said: meaning the mother of Ibrahim, son of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)"
"9764","He said: my uncle Wahb ibn Nafi informed me, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote to Urwah ibn Muhammad to demolish the churches in the towns of the Muslims. He said: so I witnessed Urwah ibn Muhammad ride until he stood at them, then he called me, and I witnessed the letter of Umar, and Urwah demolished them"
"9765","Mamar informed us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, he informed him: that he passed with Hisham by Hiddah, where a church had newly been built, so he consulted about demolishing it, and Hisham demolished it"
"9766","Umar informed us, from a man, from one who heard al-Hasan saying: it is of the Sunnah that the churches in the towns, old and new, be demolished"
"9767","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, from a shaykh of the people of Madinah called Hanash Abu Ali, from Ikrimah the freedman of Ibn Abbas, he said: Ibn Abbas was asked: may the polytheists build churches in the land of the Arabs? Ibn Abbas said: as for what the Muslims have founded as towns, no church, synagogue, fire-temple, cross may be raised in it, no horn may be blown in it, no clapper struck in it, no wine or pig may enter it. And whatever land was conciliated by treaty, the Muslims must fulfill their treaty to them. He said: the meaning of what the Muslims founded: whatever was of the land of the Arabs, or was taken from the land of the polytheists by force"
"9768","Mamar informed us, from Zayd ibn Rafi, from Haram ibn Muawiyah, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to us: let no pig be near you, let no cross be raised among you, do not eat at a table upon which wine is drunk, train horses, and walk between the two targets"
"9769","Mamar informed us, from Amr ibn Maymun ibn Mihran, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote that the Christians in Syria be prevented from striking clappers, he said: and that they be forbidden to part their heads (in Christian fashion), to cut their forelocks, to fasten girdles, to ride on saddles, to wear turbans, and to raise their crosses above their churches; if any of them is found doing any of that after warning, his spoil belongs to whoever finds him. He said: and he wrote that their women be prevented from riding litters. Amr ibn Maymun said: and Umar consulted me about demolishing their churches, so I said: do not demolish them; this is what peace was made upon with them, so Umar left them"
"9770","Al-Thawri informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabus ibn al-Mukhariq, from his father, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr wrote to Ali asking him about a Muslim who committed adultery with a Christian woman, so he wrote to him: establish the hadd of Allah upon the Muslim, and hand the Christian woman to her co-religionists"
"9771","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: the hadds apply to the people of the covenant; when they are among us their hadd is as the hadd of the Muslim. From Ismail ibn Muhammad and Yaqub ibn Utbah. Ibn Jurayj said: and Ata said to me: and we have the choice, if we wish we judge between the People of the Book, and if we wish we turn away and do not judge between them; if we judge between them, we judge with our judgment among ourselves, or we leave them to their own judgment among themselves. That is His saying: so judge between them or turn away from them"
"9772","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri: that so judge between them or turn away from them, he said: the Sunnah has passed that they be referred in their rights and inheritances to their co-religionists, except that they come desiring a hadd that we judge between them in, then we judge between them by the Book of Allah. And Allah the Mighty and Majestic said to His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): and if you judge, judge between them with justice"
"9773","Al-Thawri informed us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim and Amir, they said concerning the People of the Book when they bring their case to Muslim judges, they said: if the governor wishes he judges between them, and if he wishes he turns away from them; if he judges between them, he judges with what Allah sent down"
"9774","Mamar informed us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote to Adi ibn Artah: when the People of the Book come to you, judge between them"
"9775","From al-Thawri, from al-Suddi, from Ikrimah, he said: this verse, so judge between them or turn away from them, was abrogated by His saying: and judge between them by what Allah sent down"
"9776","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: they said: if a man of the People of the Book commits adultery with a Muslim woman, or steals something from a Muslim, the hadd is established upon him, and the Imam does not turn away from that. He says: in everything between the Muslims and the People of the Book the Imam does not turn away"
"9777","Mamar informed us, he said: I heard al-Zuhri saying: there is no hadd upon one who accuses a Jew or Christian (of adultery)"
"9778","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah informed me, he said: I asked my father: is there a hadd upon one who slanders the dhimmis? He said: I do not see a hadd upon him. Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Nafi saying: there is no hadd upon him"
"9779","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad and Yaqub ibn Utbah, they said: they claimed there is no hadd upon one who accuses them, except that the ruler disciplines"
"9780","From al-Thawri, from Tariq ibn Abd al-Rahman and Mutarrif ibn Tarif, they said: we were with al-Shabi when two men, a Muslim and a Christian, were brought to him, each having slandered the other. So he flogged the Christian eighty for the Muslim, and said to the Christian: what is in you is greater than the slander of this one, so he left him (unpunished for slandering the Muslim's accuser). That was raised to Abd al-Hamid ibn Zayd, who wrote about it to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, mentioning what al-Shabi had done, and Umar wrote approving what al-Shabi had done. Al-Thawri said: whoever slanders a Christian, there is no hadd upon him. And he said concerning a Christian who slanders a Christian: some of them are not flogged for others, and if they seek judgment from the Muslims, just as a Muslim is not flogged for them when he slanders them, likewise some of them are not flogged for others"
"9781","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ismail and Yaqub and others, they said: their sorcerer is not killed. They claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had some of that done to him, yet the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not kill its doer, and he was of the people of the covenant"
"9782","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that the Jews of Banu Zurayq bewitched the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was not mentioned that he killed any of them"
"9783","Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Kab ibn Malik, that a Jewish woman gave the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a roasted sheep at Khaybar. He said to her: what is this? She said: a gift, being careful not to say charity lest he not eat it. So he ate it and his companions ate, then he said to them: hold back. He said to the woman: did you poison this sheep? She said: yes. She said: who told you? He said: this bone of its leg, while it was in his hand. She said: yes. He said: why? She said: I thought if you are a liar the people would be relieved of you, and if you are a prophet it would not harm you. He said: and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cupped on the upper back and ordered that they be cupped, and some of them died. Al-Zuhri said: and she became Muslim so he left her. Mamar said: as for the people, they mention that he killed her"
"9784","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata said to me: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight the people until they say: there is no god but Allah; when they say: there is no god but Allah, they protect their blood and properties except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah"
"9785","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I was commanded to fight the people until they say: there is no god but Allah; when they do that they protect from me their blood and properties except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah"
"9786","Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, he said: when Abu Bakr resolved to fight the apostates, Umar said to him: how do you fight the people, O Abu Bakr, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight the people until they say: there is no god but Allah; when they say it they protect from me their blood and properties except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah? Abu Bakr said: by Allah, I shall fight whoever separates prayer from zakat, for zakat is the right of property; by Allah, had they withheld from me a young goat they used to give to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I would have fought them over it. Umar said: by Allah, it was only that I saw Allah had opened the breast of Abu Bakr to fighting, so I knew it was the truth"
"9787","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I asked Ata: are the Magians People of the Book? He said: No. I said: then the Asbidhiyyun? He said: the letter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to them was found, they claimed, after Umar ibn al-Khattab wanted to take the jizyah from them; when he found it he left them. He said: so they claimed that"
"9788","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Bajalah al-Tamimi, that Umar ibn al-Khattab did not want to take the jizyah from the Magians until Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf testified that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it from the Magians of Hajar"
"9789","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab went out and passed by some companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among them Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and said: I do not know what to do about these people who are neither Arabs nor People of the Book, meaning the Magians. Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: follow with them the practice of the People of the Book"
"9790","Ibn Jurayj said: and Jafar ibn Muhammad informed us, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to the people of Hajar: you have that no doer of good shall bear the sin of an evildoer, and had I truly fought you I would have expelled you from Hajar"
"9791","Mamar informed us, he said: I asked al-Zuhri: is the jizyah taken from those who are not People of the Book? He said: Yes; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it from the people of Bahrain, Umar from the people of the Sawad, and Uthman from the Berbers"
"9792","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Yaqub ibn Utbah and Ismail ibn Muhammad and others, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the jizyah from the Magians of Hajar, and that Umar ibn al-Khattab took from the Magians of the Sawad, and that Uthman took from the Berbers"
"9793","From al-Thawri, from Qays ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to the Magians of Hajar calling them to Islam: whoever becomes Muslim, the truth is accepted from him, and whoever refuses, the jizyah is imposed upon him; their slaughtered animals are not eaten, and no woman of them is married"
"9794","From Ibn Uyaynah, from a shaykh of theirs called Abu Sad, from a man who witnessed that, I think Nasr ibn Asim, that al-Mustawrid ibn Alqamah was in a gathering, or Farwah ibn Nawfal al-Ashjai, when a man said: there is no jizyah upon the Magians. Al-Mustawrid said: you say this, yet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it from the Magians of Hajar; by Allah, what you conceal is more wicked than what you show. So he took him until he entered upon Ali, while he was in a palace sitting in a dome, and said: O Commander of the Believers, this one claims there is no jizyah upon the Magians, yet I know the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it from the Magians of Hajar. Ali said: sit down, he says: sit down; by Allah, there is no one on earth today more knowledgeable about that than me. The Magians were People of the Book who knew it and studied knowledge, then a chief of theirs drank wine and became drunk and fell upon his sister; a group of Muslims saw him. In the morning his sister said: you did such and such with her, and a group saw you who will not conceal for you. So he summoned the greedy people and gave them, then said to them: you know that Adam married his sons to his daughters. Then those who had seen him came and said: woe to the far one, upon your back is a hadd of Allah. So those with him killed them. Then a woman came and said to him: rather I saw you. He said to her: woe to the prostitute of Banu so-and-so. She said: yes, by Allah, she was a prostitute then repented. So he killed her. Then what was in their hearts and their books was taken away, and nothing remained sound with them"
"9795","Mamar informed us, from Qatadah and others, that twenty-four dirhams per year were taken from the Magians of Bahrain for every man"
"9796","Al-Thawri informed us, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from al-Shabi, he said: the people of the Sawad had no covenant; when the kharaj was taken from them, they had a covenant"
"9797","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I said to Ata: the Christians of the Arabs? He said: Muslims may not marry their women, nor are their slaughtered animals eaten. He used to consider Jews only the Children of Israel at all, and when asked about the Christians likewise. And when you asked him about the sadaqat of their properties, how they are taken, he gave them the status of the People of the Book"
"9798","Ibn Jurayj said, from Abd al-Karim, he said: they say from Ali: the women of the Arab Christians may not be married, nor their slaughtered animals eaten"
"9799","Mamar said, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abidah al-Salmani, that Ali used to dislike the slaughtered animals of the Christians of Banu Taghlib, saying: they hold to nothing of Christianity except drinking wine"
"9800","Al-Thawri informed us, from Yunus, from Ibn Sirin, from Abidah, from Ali, he said: the slaughtered animals of the Arab Christians are not eaten, for they hold to nothing of Christianity except drinking wine. From Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abidah, from Ali, the same"
"9801","Al-Thawri informed us, from Asim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: and whoever takes them as allies among you, then he is of them"
"9802","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: there is no harm in their slaughtered animals"
"9803","Al-Thawri informed us, from Abu Husayn, from al-Shabi, he said: Allah made their slaughtered animals lawful, and your Lord is never forgetful"
"9804","Mamar informed us, he said: I asked al-Zuhri about the slaughtered animals of the Arab Christians, and he said: there is no harm in them; whoever professes a religion is of its people. He said: and their women may be married"
"9805","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab said to me: whoever of the Arabs enters (their religion) is in their religion; he is entangled"
"9806","From Mamar, from Ata al-Khurasani, he said: there is no harm in their slaughtered animals; do you not hear Allah saying: and among them are unlettered ones who do not know the Book"
"9807","Al-Thawri informed us, from Abu al-Ala Burd ibn Sinan, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, he said: the governor of Umar wrote that before us are people called the Samaritans who read the Torah, keep the Sabbath, and do not believe in resurrection; what does the Commander of the Believers think about their slaughtered animals? Umar wrote to him: they are a sect of the People of the Book; their slaughtered animals are as the slaughtered animals of the People of the Book"
"9808","Al-Thawri informed us, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Ala, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, he said: it reached Umar that his officials take wine as jizyah, so he adjured them three times. Bilal said: they do that. He said: do not do it, but let them sell it (themselves); for the Jews were forbidden fats, yet they sold them and ate their prices"
"9809","Al-Thawri informed us, from Mansur, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, he said: Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: when Allah sent down Surah al-Baqarah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and recited it, then he forbade trade in wine"
"9810","Ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: it reached Umar that Samurah sold wine, so he said: may Allah curse Samurah; does he not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: may Allah curse the Jews, fats were forbidden to them yet they melted them and sold them. He melted them: he rendered them"
"9811","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from a man, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw Umar turning his palms and saying: may Allah curse Samurah, a petty laborer of ours in Iraq; he mixed into the fay of the Muslims a price for us of wine and pork, yet they are unlawful and their price is unlawful"
"9812","Al-Thawri informed us concerning a Christian who advanced a loan to a Christian in wine, then one of them became Muslim, he said: he takes his principal. If one of them lends the other wine and the lender becomes Muslim, he takes nothing; and if the borrower becomes Muslim, he returns to the Christian the price of the wine"
"9813","Al-Thawri informed us, from Mansur, from Fudayl, from Ibrahim, that a Muslim man bought wine before it was forbidden; when it was forbidden, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: spill it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, it belongs to orphans. He said: spill it. So he spilled it until it flowed in the valley"
"9814","Mamar informed us, from Qatadah and Thabit and Aban, all of them from Anas ibn Malik, he said: a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have an orphan's property with me and I bought wine with it; do you permit me to sell it and return the orphan's property to him? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: may Allah curse the Jews, fats were forbidden to them yet they sold them and ate their prices. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not permit him to sell wine"
"9815","Ubaydillah ibn Umar informed us, from Nafi, from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, and Mamar, from Nafi, from Safiyyah, she said: Umar found wine in the house of a man of Thaqif, and he had already flogged him for wine, so he burned his house and said: what is your name? He said: Ruwayshid. He said: rather you are Fuwaysiq"
"9816","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata was asked about a Magian who combined a woman and her daughter (in marriage), then became Muslim. He said: it is more beloved to me that he keep away from both"
"9817","Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, concerning a Magian who combined a woman and her daughter, then they became Muslim: he parts from both together, and may never marry either of them"
"9818","Al-Thawri informed us, from Jabir al-Jufi, from al-Shabi, he said: what is forbidden in the lawful is more strictly (forbidden) in the unlawful. Al-Thawri said concerning a man who combined two Magian sisters then they became Muslim, he said: in Islam he parts from both sisters"
"9819","Al-Thawri informed us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, concerning one who deliberately marries a Magian woman in her waiting period, he said: there is no hadd upon him"
"9820","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, he said: there is no harm in marrying women of the People of the Book, but the women of the Arab Christians may not be married"
"9821","Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, that Hudhayfah married a Jewish woman in the time of Umar, so Umar said: divorce her, for she is an ember. He said: is she unlawful? He said: No. So Hudhayfah did not divorce her at his word, until after that he divorced her"
"9822","Al-Thawri informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote that the Muslim marries the Christian woman, while the Christian may not marry the Muslim woman"
"9823","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amir ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nistas informed me that Talhah ibn Ubaydillah married the daughter of the chief of the Jews. He said: so Umar insisted upon him that he divorce her"
"9824","Al-Thawri informed us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, that Talhah ibn Ubaydillah married a Jewish woman"
"9825","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: there is no harm in marrying them"
"9826","Al-Thawri informed us: there is no harm in combining four of the People of the Book"
"9827","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyab: that the woman of the People of the Book, her waiting period, divorce and division (of nights) are as the condition of the Muslims"
"9828","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, that he used to say: the woman of the People of the Book is as the free Muslim woman; her waiting period, divorce, and division for her, when she is with a Muslim woman. He said: and she may be married alongside a Muslim woman, and whoever marries her has become chaste; they were named chaste women"
"9829","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa said to me: the case of the Jewish and Christian woman with them in Syria is as the case of the free Muslim woman, in divorce, waiting period, and division between her and the free Muslim woman"
"9830","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, concerning His saying: and the chaste women of those given the Book, he said: when she guards her chastity and bathes from major impurity"
"9831","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I said: a woman of the People of the Book (wed) to a Magian, marriage or sale? He said: I do not like that"
"9832","Al-Thawri informed us, from Layth, from Ata, that he disliked a Christian woman to be with a Magian, and disliked that a Christian woman be sold"
"9833","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he heard him saying concerning a man who has a Muslim slave-girl and a Christian slave: may he marry the slave to the slave-girl? He said: No"
"9834","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a Christian woman under a Christian man who becomes Muslim before he consummates with her, he said: she parts from him and she has no dowry. Al-Thawri informed us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, the same. Al-Thawri said: and others said: she has half the dowry, because she called him to Islam"
"9835","Rabah informed us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, he said: she parts from him, and she has half the dowry"
"9836","From Rabah, from Mamar, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning a Christian woman under a Christian man who becomes Muslim before he consummates with her, he said: they are separated, with no dowry"
"9837","Al-Thawri informed us concerning a polytheist who divorced a polytheist woman, and she had not completed her waiting period when she became Muslim, he said: she observes three menstrual cycles. He said: and she has no inheritance. And he said concerning a polytheist who died leaving a polytheist wife, and she became Muslim before her waiting period ended, he said: she observes three months and ten (days), counting what passed of her waiting period in polytheism before becoming Muslim"
"9838","From al-Thawri, he said: if the two are belligerents and one of them becomes Muslim, the marriage is severed"
"9839","Mamar informed us, from Amr, from al-Hasan, he said: when the apostate apostatizes from Islam, what is between him and his wife is severed. Al-Thawri said: the man and woman are alike"
"9840","Al-Thawri said: if the woman apostatizes, having a husband who has not consummated with her, she has no dowry, and what is between them is severed; if he had consummated with her, she has the full dowry"
"9841","Mamar informed us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said concerning a man taken captive who becomes Christian, he said: when that is known, his wife is quit of him and observes three menstrual cycles"
"9842","Al-Thawri informed us, from Musa ibn Abi Kathir, he said: I asked Ibn al-Musayyab about the apostate: how long does his wife observe? He said: three menstrual cycles. I said: he was killed? He said: four months and ten (days)"
"9843","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Karim al-Basri, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said concerning a Christian woman under a Christian man, when the woman becomes Muslim, he said: a Christian may not be over a Muslim woman; they are separated"
"9844","Al-Thawri informed us, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, he said: the son of the woman between whom Umar separated informed me, when Islam was presented to him (the husband) and he refused, so he (Umar) separated them"
"9845","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: the women of the People of the Book are lawful for us, and our women are unlawful for them"
"9846","Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abdillah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi, he said: a woman of al-Hirah became Muslim while her husband did not become Muslim, so Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote about her: give her the choice; if she wishes she parts from him, and if she wishes she remains with him"
"9847","Ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, that Ali said: he has more right to her as long as he does not remove her from her town"
"9848","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: he has more right to her as long as he does not remove her from her land of emigration"
"9849","Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, he said: a woman of the People of the Book may be married only under covenant"
"9850","Al-Hasan ibn Umarah informed us, from al-Hakam, from Abu Iyad, from Ali, concerning marrying polytheist women outside covenant, that he disliked their women, and permitted their slaughtered animals in the land of war. From al-Thawri, from one of his companions, from al-Hakam, from Abu Iyad, the same"
"9851","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: it reached me that a woman of the People of the Book may be married only under covenant"
"9852","Abdillah ibn Umar informed us, from Nafi, from Aslam the freedman of Umar, that Umar wrote to the commanders of the armies: do not impose the jizyah upon women nor children, and impose the jizyah upon every man puberty has come upon; seal their necks, cut their forelocks of whoever of them grows hair, bind them with girdles, and forbid them riding except on packsaddles sideways. He said, meaning: his two legs on one side. Abdillah said: and Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz did that with them when he ruled"
"9853","Abdillah said: in the report of Nafi, from Aslam: so Umar imposed the jizyah upon those in Syria among them, four dinars upon every man, two mudds of food, and two or three qists of oil; upon those in Egypt, four dinars, two irdabbs of food, and something he mentioned; upon those in Iraq, forty dirhams and fifteen qafizes, and something I do not remember; upon them with that, hospitality of every Muslim passing by them for three days; and he imposed garments upon them, and mentioned something he did not remember"
"9854","Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made peace with the idol-worshippers on the jizyah, except whoever of them was of the Arabs; and he accepted the jizyah from the people of Bahrain, who were Magians"
"9855","Al-Aslami informed me, from Abu al-Huwayrith, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) imposed upon a Christian in Makkah called Mawhib a dinar every year as jizyah. He said: and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) imposed upon the people of Aylah three hundred dinars every year, and upon them hospitality of every Muslim passing by them for three (days), and that they deceive no Muslim. Ibrahim said: so Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Farwah informed me: that they were three hundred"
"9856","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I asked Ata about the jizyah, and he said: we know nothing fixed except what they were conciliated upon; then they protected everything of their properties. He said: and Amr ibn Dinar said that to me"
"9857","Ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, he said: I said to Mujahid: what is the matter of the people of Syria of the People of the Book, four dinars are taken from them in the jizyah, and from the people of Yemen a dinar? He said: that is due to affluence"
"9858","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, from Nafi, that he told him, from Umar ibn al-Khattab: that he imposed the jizyah upon every man who reached puberty, forty dirhams or four dinars; he put silver upon those of them in Iraq, for it is a land of silver, and put gold upon the people of Syria, for it is a land of gold; and he imposed upon them with that their provisions and the clothing with which Umar used to clothe the people, and hospitality of every Muslim lodging with them for three nights and their days"
"9859","He said: Ibn Jurayj, and Musa said to us, Nafi said: so I heard Aslam the freedman of Umar narrating, from Ibn Umar: that the people of the jizyah of Syria came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: when the Muslims lodge with us they burden us with sheep and chickens. Umar said: feed them of your food which you eat, and do not add for them beyond that"
"9860","Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Aslam the freedman of Umar: that Umar imposed the jizyah and wrote thereby to the commanders of the armies not to impose the jizyah except upon whom puberty has come, nor impose it upon a child nor a woman. So he imposed upon the people of Iraq forty dirhams upon every man, and upon the people of Iraq also fifteen sas; upon the people of Syria four dinars upon every man, and upon the people of Syria also two mudds of wheat, three qists of oil, and so-and-so amount of honey and fat, which Ayyub or Nafi did not remember; upon the people of Egypt four dinars upon every man, and upon the people of Egypt also an irdabb of wheat and something he does not remember, and the clothing of the Commander of the Believers as an imposed levy; and upon them hospitality of the Muslims for three (days), feeding them of what they eat of what is lawful for the Muslims of their food. When Umar came to Syria they complained to him that they burden us with chickens, so Umar said: feed them only of what you eat of what is lawful for them of your food"
"9861","Ma'mar reported from Abu Ishaq, he said: A stipulation upon them of one day and one night of hospitality."
"9862","Hushaym ibn Bashir reported from Abu Bishr Ja'far ibn Wahshiyyah, from Mujahid, that Umar imposed upon those in Yemen from the Ahl al-Dhimmah a dinar upon every adult, and upon those in Sham from the Romans four dinars, and upon the people of al-Sawad forty-eight dirhams."
"9863","Ma'mar reported from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Masruq ibn al-Ajda', he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent Mu'adh ibn Jabal to Yemen, and ordered him to take from every adult male of the Ahl al-Dhimmah a dinar or its value in Mu'afiri cloth. Abd al-Razzaq said: Ma'mar used to say: This is a mistake, his saying female adult: there is nothing upon women, Ma'mar is the speaker. Al-Thawri said: Concerning one of the Ahl al-Dhimmah who is needy and does not find what to pay of his jizyah, he said: He is granted respite until he finds and pays, and there is nothing else upon him; if he becomes well-off it is taken for what passed, and if he is unable to pay anything of the settlement he agreed upon, it is remitted from him when his inability is known, and the Imam remits it from him."
"9864","Ibn Jurayj said: It was in the letter of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to the people of Yemen: Whoever dislikes Islam among the Jews and Christians, he is not turned away from his religion, and upon him is the jizyah, upon every adult, male and female, free and slave, a dinar or of the value of Mu'afiri cloth or its goods. Al-Thawri said: There is mentioned from Umar different levies upon the Ahl al-Dhimmah who were taken by force. Al-Thawri said: That is up to the governor: he increases upon them by an amount that pleases them, and reduces from them according to their need, and there is no fixed time for it; the governor considers according to what they can bear. As for what was not taken by force such that they were conciliated by a settlement, nothing is added upon them beyond what they were settled upon, and the jizyah is according to what they were settled upon, little or much, upon their lands and their persons. He says: There is no zakah upon them in their wealth."
"9865","Ibn Jurayj said: Sulayman al-Ahwal informed me, from Tawus, he said: When two jizyah payments accumulate upon men, the first is taken."
"9866","Ma'mar reported from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'sa'ah ibn Mu'awiyah, that he asked Ibn Abbas and said: We pass by the Ahl al-Dhimmah and they slaughter for us chicken and sheep. He said: And what do you say? He said: What? He said: He says: There is no way against the unlettered ones. He said: When they pay the jizyah, their wealth is not lawful to you except with their willing consent."
"9867","From Ibn Abi Rawwad: An army passed by the crop of a man from the Ahl al-Dhimmah, and they released their mounts into it, but one man of them restrained his mount and kept following the pasture with it and preventing it from the crop. Then the dhimmi owner of the crop came to the one who restrained his mount and said: May Allah suffice me through you, or he said: May Allah suffice me by you; were it not for you I would have been spared these, but these are only warded off by you."
"9868","Al-Thawri reported from al-A'mash and Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Sa'id ibn Wahb, he said: We were with a commander from the commanders, and he saw us refraining from taking of the fruit of the Ahl al-Dhimmah, and said: Among what Umar settled with them is one day and one night for the traveller, meaning lodging."
"9869","Al-Thawri reported from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from a man from Juhaynah from the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: That the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Perhaps you will fight a people and prevail over them, and they will shield themselves from you with their wealth apart from their persons and their sons, and make peace with you, so do not take from them other than that."
"9870","Al-Thawri reported from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A'la, he said: I said to Sa'id ibn Jubayr: I pass by fruits, may I eat of them? He said: No, except with the permission of their owners. Ibn Jurayj said: It is not proper for a Muslim to give the jizyah, affirming humiliation and disgrace. He said: And I heard more than one saying that."
"9871","Al-Thawri reported from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, and a man came to him and said: I take land, I lease it, a jizyah land, and I cultivate it and pay its kharaj? He forbade him, then another came to him and he forbade him, then another came to him and he forbade him, then he said: Do not deliberately take what Allah has placed upon this disbeliever and remove it from his neck and place it upon your neck. Then he recited: Fight those who do not believe in Allah nor in the Last Day, until humbled."
"9872","Al-Thawri reported from Kulayb ibn Wa'il, he said: I asked Ibn Umar, he said: I said: What is your view on buying land? He said: Good. He said: They take from me for every jarib a qafiz and a dirham. He said: Do not place humiliation upon your neck."
"9873","From al-Thawri, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Maymun ibn Mihran, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I do not like that all the land be mine as jizyah for five dirhams, affirming humiliation upon myself. Abdullah ibn Muharrar reported, he said: Maymun ibn Mihran informed me, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying the like of it."
"9874","Ma'mar reported from Ayyub that a man from Najran became Muslim, and they wanted to take jizyah from me on his account, or as he said, but he refused. Then Umar ibn al-Khattab said: You are only one seeking refuge. The man said: In Islam there is indeed refuge if you do it. Then Umar said: You spoke the truth; by Allah, in Islam there is indeed refuge."
"9875","Ma'mar reported from Ayyub, from Anas ibn Sirin, he said: Anas ibn Malik employed me over al-Aylah, and I said: You employed me over tax collection from your work. He said: Take what Umar ibn al-Khattab used to take from the Muslims: when it reached two hundred dirhams, of every forty dirhams a dirham; and from the Ahl al-Dhimmah of every twenty dirhams a dirham; and from one who is not from the Ahl al-Dhimmah of every ten dirhams a dirham."
"9876","Hisham ibn Hassan reported from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, that he sent him over al-Aylah. He said: I said: You sent me over the worst of your work. He said: Then he brought out to me the letter of Umar ibn al-Khattab, then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Ma'mar."
"9877","Ma'mar reported from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab decreed concerning the wealth of the Ahl al-Dhimmah, when they pass with it by the collectors of sadaqah, half the tenths; and concerning the wealth of the polytheist traders who were from the Ahl al-Dhimmah, half the tenth."
"9878","Al-Thawri reported from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, that he heard Ziyad ibn Hudayr, he said: The first tithe-collector to collect tithes in Islam was I, and we did not tithe a Muslim nor a covenanted one. He said: I said: Whom did you tithe? He said: The Christians of Banu Taghlib. Ibrahim said: Then a man narrated to me from Ziyad, he said: I said to him: And how much did you tithe them? He said: Half the tenth."
"9879","Ibn Jurayj reported from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Zurayq, the collector of the taxes of Egypt, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote to him: Whoever passes by you of the Muslims having wealth with which he trades, take from him his sadaqah, of every forty dinars a dinar; what falls short of that down to twenty, then by proportion of that down to ten dinars; if it falls short by a third of a dinar, take nothing from him. And whoever passes by you of the People of the Book or of the Ahl al-Dhimmah who trade, take from him of every twenty dinars a dinar; what falls short, then by proportion of that down to ten dinars; if it falls short by a third of a dinar, take nothing from him."
"9880","Ibn Jurayj said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed me also that the first who took half the tenths from the Ahl al-Dhimmah when they traded was Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he used to take from the Nabataean traders, the people of Sham, when they came to Madinah."
"9881","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Shu'ayb said: The people of Manbij and those beyond the sea of Aden wrote to Umar ibn al-Khattab offering him that they enter with their trade into the land of the Arabs, with the tenths thereof for him. Umar consulted about that the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and they agreed upon that. He was the first who took the tenths from them."
"9882","Ma'mar reported from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: There is taken from the People of the Book double what is taken from the Muslims, from the people of gold and silver. He said: Umar ibn al-Khattab did that, and Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz."
"9883","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: There is no sadaqah in the wealth of the Ahl al-Dhimmah, except that they pass by the tithe-collector and he takes from them of every twenty dinars a dinar."
"9884","Ibn Uyaynah reported from Ibn Abi Najih, he said: Umar asked the Muslims: How do the Abyssinians treat you when you enter their land? They said: They take a tenth of what is with us. He said: Take from them the like of what they take from you."
"9885","Ma'mar reported from Ibn Tawus, from his father, that Ibn Abbas was asked by Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, and Ibrahim was a governor at Aden, and he said to Ibn Abbas: What is due in the wealth of the Ahl al-Dhimmah? He said: Pardon. He said: I said: They order us with such and such. He said: Do not act for them. He said: What is due in ambergris? He said: If there is anything in it, then the fifth."
"9886","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz took from the Muslim traders of every forty dinars a dinar."
"9887","Al-Thawri said: Khalid ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, from Ziyad ibn Hudayr, he said: We used to collect tithes in the governorship of Umar ibn al-Khattab, and we did not tithe a covenanted one nor a Muslim. He said: I said to him: Whom did you tithe? He said: The traders of the people of war, as they tithe us when we come to them. He said: And Ziyad ibn Hudayr was a governor for Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"9888","Abdullah ibn Kathir reported from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, he said: I heard Ibrahim al-Nakha'i narrating from Ziyad ibn Hudayr, and Ziyad was then alive, that Umar sent him as a sadaqah collector, and ordered him to take from the Christians of Banu Taghlib the tenth, and from the Christians of the Arabs half the tenth."
"9889","Ma'mar reported from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that Umar used to take from the Nabataeans from wheat and oil the tenth, intending thereby to increase the carrying to Madinah, and he took from legumes half the tenth, meaning chickpeas and lentils and what resembles them."
"9890","Abdullah ibn Umar reported from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: He was asked about the polytheists, what is taken from them when they trade in the land of the Muslims? Umar said: What they take from you, except of oil and wheat, then take from them half the tenth, intending that they carry that to them."
"9891","Ma'mar reported from Qatadah, from Abu Mijlaz: That Umar ibn al-Khattab sent Ammar ibn Yasir, Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, and Uthman ibn Hunayf to Kufah. He made Ammar over prayer and fighting, and made Abdullah ibn Mas'ud over judiciary and the treasury, and made Uthman ibn Hunayf over land survey. He assigned them each day a sheep: half of it and its offal for Ammar, a quarter for Ibn Mas'ud, and a quarter for Uthman ibn Hunayf. Then he said: I do not see a town from which a sheep is taken every day but that will quickly affect it. Then he said to them: I have placed you and myself with regard to this wealth like the guardian of the orphan: Whoever is rich, let him abstain, and whoever is poor, let him eat in a fair manner. He said: Then Uthman apportioned upon every head of the Ahl al-Dhimmah twenty-four dirhams every year, and did not impose upon women and children anything of that; and he surveyed the Sawad of Kufah of the land of the Ahl al-Dhimmah, and placed upon the jarib of date-palms ten dirhams, upon the jarib of grapes eight dirhams, upon the jarib of reeds six dirhams, upon the jarib of wheat four dirhams, and upon the jarib of barley two dirhams; and he took from the traders of the Ahl al-Dhimmah of every twenty dirhams a dirham. He raised that to Umar and he was pleased with it."
"9892","From Ma'mar, from Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, that a man became Muslim in the time of Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: Remove the jizyah from my land. Umar said: Your land was taken by force."
"9893","Ma'mar reported from Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Ibrahim, he said: A man came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: The people of such and such land can bear of kharaj more than is upon them. He said: There is no way to them; they were only conciliated by a settlement."
"9894","Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Tanukhi reported, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to me, he said: I had land with its jizyah, and my governor wrote concerning it to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz. Umar wrote: Take the jizyah and the tenths, then take from him the surplus. He said: Meaning, whichever of them was greater."
"9895","Al-Thawri reported from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote concerning a dihqanah from the people of Nahr al-Malik who became Muslim, and she had much land, and he wrote concerning her to Umar. He wrote: Hand over to her her land, and she pays kharaj for it."
"9896","Al-Thawri reported from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, that al-Rufayl, the dihqan of the two rivers of Karbala, became Muslim, and Umar assigned him two thousand, and handed over to him his land, he paying kharaj for it."
"9897","Hushaym ibn Bashir reported, he said: Sayyar Abu al-Hakam informed me, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, that Ali ibn Abi Talib said to a dihqan: If you become Muslim, I will remove the dinar from your head, and take it from your wealth."
"9898","Ibn Uyaynah reported from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, he said: I heard Umar, four days before his killing, while standing upon his mount over Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman and Uthman ibn Hunayf, say: See what is before you, lest you have burdened the land with what it cannot bear. Hudhayfah said: We burdened the land with a matter it can bear, and I left for them the like of what I took from them. Uthman ibn Hunayf said: I burdened the land with a matter it can bear, and I left for them a small surplus. He said: See what is before you, lest you have burdened the land with what it cannot bear; if Allah spares me, I shall leave the widows of the people of Iraq needing no one after me."
"9899","Ibn Uyaynah reported from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid: Whatever city is conquered by force, its people are slaves and their wealth is for the poor; if they become Muslim before they are divided, they are free and their wealth is for the poor."
"9900","Ma'mar reported from Hammam ibn Munabbih, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whatever town you come to, your share is in it, or a word resembling it; and whatever town disobeys Allah and His Messenger, its land is for Allah and His Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then it is yours."
"9901","Ma'mar reported from al-A'mash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, he said: An old man who had been Christian then became Muslim, then apostatized from Islam, was brought to Ali. Ali said to him: Perhaps you apostatized only to obtain an inheritance then return to Islam? He said: No. He said: Perhaps you proposed to a woman and they refused to marry her to you, so you intended to marry her then return to Islam? He said: No. He said: Return to Islam. He said: Not until I meet Christ, no. Then Ali ordered concerning him and his neck was struck, and his inheritance was handed to his Muslim children."
"9902","Ibn Jurayj reported from one who narrated to him, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, that al-Mustawrid al-Ijli apostatized from Islam, and Ali asked him to repent but he refused to repent. He killed him and divided his wealth among his heirs, and ordered his wife to observe waiting period of four months and ten days."
"9903","Ma'mar reported from a man, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, that Ibn Mas'ud judged in the inheritance of the apostate with the like of the saying of Ali. Ibn Jurayj said the like of it from Ibn Mas'ud."
"9904","Ma'mar reported from Ishaq ibn Rashid, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote concerning a man captured who became Christian, of the Muslims: When that is known, his wife is quit of him and observes waiting period of three menstrual cycles from him, and his wealth is handed to his Muslim heirs."
"9905","Al-Thawri reported concerning the apostate when he is killed: His wealth is for his heirs; and when he joins the land of war, his wealth is for the Muslims. I do not know him but he said: Except that he have an heir upon his religion in the land of war, then he is more entitled to it."
"9906","Abdullah ibn Kathir reported from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, that Ali said: The inheritance of the apostate is for his children."
"9907","From al-Thawri, from Musa ibn Abi Kathir, he said: I asked Ibn al-Musayyab about the apostate: How long does his wife observe waiting period? He said: Three menstrual cycles. He said: I said: He was killed. He said: Then four months and ten days. He said: I said: Is his inheritance connected? He said: His inheritance is not connected. He said: Do his sons inherit him? He said: We inherit them and they do not inherit us."
"9908","Al-Thawri reported from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: The people of polytheism, we inherit them and they do not inherit us."
"9909","Ma'mar reported from one who heard al-Hasan, he said: The inheritance of the apostate is for the Muslims, though they used to make it pleasant for his heirs."
"9910","Ma'mar reported from Qatadah, he said: His inheritance is for the people of his religion."
"9911","Ma'mar reported from a man, from al-Hasan, he said: When the apostate repents, they deem it good for him to begin anew with Hajj, if he had performed Hajj before his apostasy."
"9912","Ibn Jurayj said: People are two parties: among them one who says: The inheritance of the apostate is for the Muslims, because the moment he disbelieves it is withheld from him, and he cannot dispose of anything of it until it is seen whether he becomes Muslim or disbelieves. Among them are al-Nakha'i, al-Sha'bi, and al-Hakam ibn Utaybah; and a party says: For the people of his religion."
"9913","Ma'mar reported from Ishaq ibn Rashid and others of the people of al-Jazirah, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote: Allow the bequest of the captive."
"9914","Ma'mar reported from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, our land is a land of the People of the Book, and they eat pork, so what shall we do with their vessels and pots? He said: If you do not find other than them, rinse them, meaning wash them."
"9915","Isra'il reported, he said: Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha informed me that Ibrahim al-Nakha'i was with them among the cavalry, and there was with him a Magian woman serving him and preparing his food and drink."
"9916","Abdullah ibn Kathir reported, he heard Shu'bah saying: Al-Qasim al-A'raj informed me that Sa'id ibn Jubayr was with them for years at Isbahan, and a Magian boy of his served him and prepared his food and drink."
"9917","Abdullah ibn Kathir reported, he heard Shu'bah saying: Al-Qasim al-A'raj informed me that Sa'id ibn Jubayr was with them for years at Isbahan, and a Magian boy of his served him and handed him the mushaf in its cover."
"9918","Ma'mar reported from Qatadah, he said: There is no harm in eating the food of the Magians except their slaughter, meaning cheese and its likes."
"9919","Humayd ibn Ruman reported from al-Hajjaj, from Ata, he said: There is no harm in eating the cheese of the Magian."
"9920","Al-Awza'i Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr reported from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Abu Kabshah, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Convey from me even a verse, and narrate from the Children of Israel and there is no harm; whoever lies upon me with a lie, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"9921","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: It was narrated to me from Zayd ibn Aslam, he said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not ask the People of the Book about anything, for they will not guide you, and they have led themselves astray. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, may we narrate from the Children of Israel? He said: Narrate and there is no harm."
"9922","Ma'mar reported from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: How do you ask the People of the Book about anything while the Book of Allah which He sent down upon you is among you pure, unmixed? It is the newest tidings from Allah, and Allah has informed you about the People of the Book, that they wrote books with their hands then said: This is from Allah, to purchase with it a small price. They altered them and distorted them from their places. Does not what came to you from Allah forbid you from asking them? By Allah, we have not seen anyone of them asking you about what was sent down to you."
"9923","Ma'mar reported from al-Zuhri, he said: Ibn Abi Namlah al-Ansari informed me that Abu Namlah informed him that: While he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a man of the Ahl al-Dhimmah came to him and said: O Muhammad, does this bier speak? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah knows best. The Jew said: It speaks. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whatever the People of the Book narrate to you, neither confirm them nor deny them, but say: We believe in Allah and His Books; if it is false you have not confirmed it, and if it is true you have not denied it."
"9924","Ma'mar reported from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Ata ibn Yasar, he said: The Jews used to narrate to the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and they would gape as if in amazement. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not confirm them nor deny them, but say: We believe in what was sent down to us and sent down to you, our God and your God is One, and we are Muslims to Him."
"9925","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Umarah, from Hurayth ibn Zahir, he said: Abdullah said: Do not ask the People of the Book about anything, for they will not guide you, and they have gone astray, lest you deny a truth and confirm a falsehood; and there is none of the People of the Book but in his heart is a remnant calling him to Allah and His Book, like the remnant of wealth. Al-taliyah is the remainder. Al-Thawri said: And Ma'n added, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah in this hadith, he said: If you must ask them, then see what agrees with the Book of Allah and take it, and what contradicts the Book of Allah, leave it."
"9926","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, that Umar ibn al-Khattab passed by a man reading a book; he listened to it a while and deemed it good. He said to the man: Do you write from this book? He said: Yes. He bought a hide for himself, then brought it to him and copied it on its front and back, then brought it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and began reading it to him, while the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, changed colour. A man of the Ansar struck the book with his hand and said: May your mother be bereaved of you, O son of al-Khattab, do you not see the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, since today while you read this book? The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said at that: I was sent as an opener and a seal, and given the comprehensive words and their openings, and speech was condensed for me in condensation, so let not the over-scrupulous destroy you."
"9927","Al-Thawri reported from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from Abdullah ibn Thabit, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I passed by a brother of mine from Qurayzah, and he wrote for me compendia of the Torah; shall I not present them to you? He said: The face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, changed. Abdullah said: I said: May Allah confound your mind, do you not see what is on the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? Umar said: I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as Prophet. He said: Then it was eased from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if Musa were among you and you followed him and left me, you would have gone astray; you are my portion of the nations, and I am your portion of the Prophets."
"9928","Ma'mar reported from al-Zuhri that Hafsah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a book of the stories of Yusuf on a shoulder-blade; she began reading it to him while the face of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, changed colour. He said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if Yusuf came to you while I am among you and you followed him and left me, you would have gone astray."
"9929","Isma'il ibn Abdullah reported from Ibn Awn, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, he said: He used to say: At Kufah was a man seeking the books of Daniel and that sort; a letter came concerning him from Umar ibn al-Khattab that he be brought to him. The man said: I do not know for what I was brought. When he came to Umar, he beat him with the stick, then began reciting to him: Alif Lam Ra, these are the verses of the clear Book, until he reached the heedless. He said: Then I knew what he wanted, and I said: O Commander of the Faithful, leave me; by Allah, I shall not leave with me anything of those books but I shall burn it. He said: Then he left him."
"9930","Al-Thawri reported from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, that a Jewish or Christian man nudged a Muslim woman then threw dust upon her, seeking her for himself. That was raised to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and Umar said: These have a covenant so long as they fulfil their covenant to you; when they do not fulfil your covenant to you, they have no covenant. He said: Then Umar crucified him."
"9931","Al-Aslami reported from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, that a Muslim woman hired a Jew or a Christian and he went with her; when they came to a hill he concealed himself with her behind it then overpowered her. Abu Salih said: I had watched her when he overpowered her, and I struck him and did not leave him until I saw that I had killed him. He said: He went to Abu Hurayrah and informed him; he summoned me and I informed him; he sent for the woman and she agreed with me upon the report. Abu Hurayrah said: Upon this we did not give you the covenant. He ordered concerning him and he was killed."
"9932","Ibn Jurayj reported, he said: One whom I trust informed me that a Jew or a Christian nudged a Muslim woman and she fell; Umar struck his neck and said: Upon this we did not make peace with you."
"9933","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed that Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah killed likewise a man of the People of the Book who sought a woman for herself; Abu Hurayrah also, and that is that a man of the People of the Book sought to strip a Muslim woman of herself while a man was watching. Abu Hurayrah asked the man where the woman could not hear, and asked the woman where the man could not hear; when they agreed he ordered his killing. It was said to me: The man was Abu Salih al-Zayyat. He said: And Abd al-Malik judged concerning a Bedouin slave-girl deflowered by a man of the People of the Book: he killed him and gave the slave-girl his wealth. Abd al-Razzaq said: And people agree that the Sunnah in this is the Sunnah of the Muslim: if he was married he is stoned, and if he was unmarried he is flogged; likewise the woman."
"9934","Ma'mar reported from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man of the Jews killed a slave-girl of the Ansar for her jewelry, then cast her into a well and crushed her head with stones. He was seized and brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he ordered concerning him that he be stoned until he die; he was stoned until he died."
"9935","Ma'mar reported from Ata al-Khurasani and al-Kalbi concerning His saying: The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger, concerning the thief who cuts the road, he is a warrior; if he kills and takes wealth, he is crucified."
"9936","Abdullah ibn Kathir reported from Shu'bah, from Mu'awiyah Abu Abdullah al-Asqalani, he said: One who saw Abdullah ibn Muhayriz informed me: He shook hands with a Christian man at Damascus."
"9937","Al-Hasan ibn Umarah reported from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, he said: They used to dislike eating with the Jews and Christians and shaking hands with them."
"9938","I heard al-Thawri and Imran: They saw no harm in shaking hands with the Jew and the Christian. Abd al-Razzaq said: And there is no harm in it."
"9939","Ma'mar reported from Abu Ishaq, from Qays ibn al-Sakan, that Ibn Mas'ud said: You have settled a land in which Muslims do not slaughter; they are only Nabataeans and Persians. When you buy meat, ask; if it is the slaughter of a Jew or a Christian, eat it, for their food is lawful to you."
"9940","And one who heard al-Hakam ibn Utaybah informed me, he says: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla informed me, from Ali, and Mujahid from Ibn Abbas, that it was said to them: The People of the Book mention other than Allah upon their slaughters. They said: When Allah permitted their slaughters He knew what they say upon their slaughters. Muqatil mentioned it."
"9941","Al-Aslami reported from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The slaughters of the People of the Book are eaten even if slaughtered for other than Allah, or he said: Even if dedicated to other than Allah."
"9942","A man reported from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: There is no harm in the slaughters of the People of the Book from the people of war, and the hunt of their dogs. Muqatil mentioned it."
"9943","Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman reported, or one who heard him narrating informed him, from Ata concerning His saying: And what is dedicated to other than Allah, if compelled, he said: He says: In the name of Christ. And he said: There is no harm in their slaughters."
"9944","Ma'mar reported from Qatadah, he said: When the Jew slaughters his slaughter and it becomes spoiled for him in his religion, it is not lawful for a Muslim to eat it."
"9945","Al-Thawri reported from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning His saying: And the food of those given the Book is lawful to you, he said: Their slaughters."
"9946","Abd al-Razzaq said: When the Christian slaughters and forgets to pronounce the name, there is no harm in it; if I hear him dedicating to other than Allah when he slaughters, I dislike it, though some of them permitted it, and I prefer that he not eat it."
"9947","One who heard Ata informed me, he says: And what is dedicated to other than Allah, Allah has permitted it, because He knew they would say this saying."
"9948","Al-Thawri reported from Mansur, from Ibrahim, that when he heard him dedicating he disliked eating it, unless he hides from him until he does not hear him. He said: His dedicating is to say: In the name of Christ."
"9949","Amr ibn Maymun said: There were people of the Christians slaughtering at Sham then selling it to the Muslims; Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz appointed over them Muslims to be present with them when they slaughter, that they pronounce Allah's name and prevent them from associating upon their slaughters."
"9950","From Ma'mar, he said: It reached me that a man asked Ibn Umar about the slaughter of the Jew and the Christian. He recited to him: Lawful to you are the good things, and the food of those given the Book is lawful to you. And he recited to him: And do not eat of that upon which Allah's name has not been mentioned. And he recited to him: And what is dedicated to other than Allah. He said: The man kept repeating to him, and Ibn Umar said: May Allah curse the Jews, the Christians, and the disbelieving Bedouins; this one and his companions ask me, and when it does not suit them they come disputing me."
"9951","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: When the Jew offers you food, order him to eat of it; if he eats, eat, and if he refuses, do not eat of it."
"9952","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, concerning a Christian who slaughtered a sheep for dyeing and erred in it deliberately until its eating became forbidden to him, he said: The Muslim shall not eat it either."
"9953","Ma'mar reported, he said: One who heard Ikrimah informed me, he saying concerning the slaughter shared between the Muslim, the Jew, and the Christian, he said: He shall not slaughter for you; slaughter yourself, for our religion overcomes their religion. Ma'mar said: I asked al-Zuhri about it, and he said: There is no harm in it; whichever of them wills, let him slaughter it. If you hear him dedicating to other than Allah, do not eat it; his dedicating is to say: In the name of Christ."
"9954","Isra'il reported, he said: Musa ibn Abi A'ishah informed me, he said: I asked Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Murrah ibn Sharaḥil about the Magian mentioning Allah's name when he slaughters. They said: Do not eat it."
"9955","Ma'mar reported from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: The slaughter of the Magian is not eaten, even if Allah's name is mentioned upon it."
"9956","Ibn Uyaynah reported from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, he said: The slaughter of the Magian is not eaten, even if Allah is mentioned."
"9957","Al-Thawri reported from Qays ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The slaughter of the Magian is not eaten."
"9958","Ma'mar reported from al-Zuhri: That the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave a kunyah to Safwan ibn Umayyah while he was then a polytheist; he came to him upon a horse, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Dismount, Abu Wahb."
"9959","Ma'mar reported from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from a man of Kalb called Ma'ruf ibn Abi Ma'ruf, from al-Farafisah al-Hanafi, from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab gave a kunyah to al-Farafisah al-Hanafi while he was Christian, saying to him: Abu Hassan. Ma'mar said: And I dislike giving a kunyah, lest he boast with the kunyah."
"9960","Ma'mar said: I said to al-Zuhri: Is it said to him: Welcome? He said: If he has a favour with you which you have not repaid, there is no harm."
"9961","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, he said: Qatadah informed me that a Christian said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I have become Muslim. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Abu al-Harith. The Christian said: I have become Muslim. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said the third time: Abu al-Harith. He said: I became Muslim before you. He said: You lie; three traits barred you from Islam: your partaking of wine, and he did not say your drinking, and your eating pork, and your claiming a son for Allah."
"9962","Ibn Uyaynah reported from Ibn Abi Najih, he said: I heard Mujahid saying to a Christian boy of his: O Jarir, become Muslim. Then he said: Thus it was said to them."
"9963","Ma'mar reported from al-Zuhri: I said to him: The Muslim frees the Christian and the Jew, is there reward in it? He said: No, and he disliked freeing them."
"9964","Al-Thawri reported from Layth, from Mujahid, that he disliked freeing the Christian."
"9965","Al-Thawri and Malik reported from Isma'il ibn Abi Hakim that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz freed a Christian boy of his."
"9966","Al-Aslami reported from Abu al-Zinad, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, that his father freed a Magian boy of his, and freed a child of adultery."
"9967","Ma'mar reported from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyab, and he was asked about the Muslim borrowing the dog of the Magian, he said: His dog is like his knife. He says: There is no harm in it."
"9968","Ma'mar reported from al-Zuhri, he said: There is no harm in it when the Muslim is the one hunting with it."
"9969","Ma'mar reported from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, that he disliked the hunt of the Magian's dog."
"9970","Ma'mar reported from Qatadah, he said: The Sabians are a people who worship the angels, pray toward the qiblah, and recite the Zabur."
"9971","Al-Thawri reported from Layth, from Mujahid, he said: The Sabians are between the Magians and the Jews; they have no religion."
"9972","Al-Hasan ibn Umarah reported from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn Abbas was asked about the Sabians, and he said: They are a people between the Jews and the Christians; their slaughters are not lawful, nor their marriage."
"9973","Ma'mar reported concerning His saying: Ask the people of remembrance if you do not know, he said: The people of the Torah; ask them: Did there come to them but men to whom revelation was given?"
"9974","Ma'mar reported from Qatadah concerning His saying: And ask those We sent before you of Our Messengers, he says: Ask the People of the Book: Did the Messengers come to them with tawhid? Did they come to them with sincerity?"
"9975","Ma'mar reported from Qatadah concerning His saying: If you are in doubt of what We sent down to you, ask those reading the Book before you, he said: It reached us that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I do not doubt, nor do I ask."
"9976","Ma'mar reported from Qatadah concerning His saying: After the guidance became clear to them, that they find him written with them."
"9977","Ibn Jurayj reported, he said: I said to Ata: The blood-money of the Magian? He said: Eight hundred dirhams."
"9978","Ma'mar reported from a man who heard Ikrimah saying: Umar decreed in the blood-money of the Magian eight hundred dirhams, and said: He is not of the People of the Book; he is only a slave."
"9979","Ibn Jurayj reported, he said: Amr ibn Shu'ayb informed me that Abu Musa wrote to Umar ibn al-Khattab that the Muslims fall upon the Magians and kill them; what is your view? Umar wrote to him: They are only slaves, so assess their value among you. Abu Musa wrote to him: Eight hundred dirhams. Umar fixed it for the Magians."
"9980","Ma'mar reported from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: The blood-money of the Magian is eight hundred dirhams. Ma'mar reported from Umar and from al-Hasan the like of it."
"9981","Ma'mar reported from Simak and others, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz made the blood-money of the Magian half the blood-money of the Muslim."
"9982","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad reported from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab made the blood-money of the Magian eight hundred dirhams."
"9983","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad reported from Ishaq ibn Muhammad, from Makhul, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, decreed in the blood-money of the Magian eight hundred dirhams."
"9984","Al-Thawri reported from Abu al-Miqdam, from Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab made the blood-money of the Jew and the Christian four thousand dirhams."
"9985","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said: The blood-money of the woman of the People of the Book is four thousand dirhams. He said: I said: Then the Christians of the Arabs? He said: Like them."
"9986","Ma'mar reported from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyab, and from Amr, from al-Hasan, they said: The blood-money of the Jew and the Christian is four thousand dirhams."
"9987","Ma'mar reported from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that a Muslim man killed a man of the Ahl al-Dhimmah deliberately; it was raised to Uthman and he did not kill him, but made the blood-money stringent upon him like the blood-money of the Muslim."
"9988","Ma'mar and al-Thawri reported from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: The blood-money of the Jew, the Christian, and the Magian is like the blood-money of the Muslim."
"9989","Ma'mar and al-Thawri reported from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: The blood-money of the dhimmi is the blood-money of the Muslim."
"9990","Al-Thawri reported from Qays ibn Muslim, from al-Sha'bi, he said: The blood-money of the Jew and the Christian is the blood-money of the Muslim."
"9991","Ma'mar reported from Qatadah, and Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, they said: The testimony of the Jew against the Christian is not allowed, nor is the testimony of the Christian against the Jew allowed; the testimony of the Christian against the Christian is allowed, and of the Jew against the Jew."
"9992","Al-Thawri reported from Abu Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, he said: The testimony of people of one creed against people of another creed is not allowed, except the Muslims."
"9993","Al-Thawri reported from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Shurayh, that he used to allow the testimony of the People of the Book, some against others."
"9994","Al-Thawri reported from Amr ibn Maymun that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz allowed the testimony of a Magian against a Christian, or a Christian against a Magian."
"9995","Al-Thawri reported from Isa, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to allow the testimony of the Christian against the Jew, and the Jew against the Christian; and Abu Husayn narrated the opposite of it."
"9996","Al-Thawri said: Concerning a man who died leaving wealth, and a Christian came and said: He is my father, he died Christian; and a Muslim came and said: He is my father, he died Muslim. He said: They only claim wealth, so the wealth is between them in halves."
"9997","Al-Thawri said: Concerning a Christian who died, and a man of the Muslims came with two witnesses of the Christians that he has upon him a thousand dirhams, and a man of the Christians came with witnesses of the Christians that he has upon him a thousand dirhams. He said: It is for the Muslim, because the testimony of the Christian harms the right of the Muslim. Al-Thawri said: Disbelief is one creed, and Islam is one creed."
"9998","Ma'mar and al-Thawri reported from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: Ka'b ibn Sur used to make the People of the Book swear, placing upon his head the Gospel, then bringing him to the altar, and he swears by Allah."
"9999","Isra'il reported, he said: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, that Abu Musa made a Jew swear by Allah. Amir said: Had you entered him into the synagogue."
"10000","Al-Thawri reported from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, he said: He used to make them swear by Allah, and he used to say: Allah sent down: And judge between them by what Allah sent down."
"10001","Ma'mar reported from al-Zuhri, he said: When the Christian woman conceives from the Muslim and dies pregnant, she is buried with the people of her religion."
"10002","Ibn Jurayj reported from Ata, he said: The people of her religion take charge of her, and she is buried with them."
"10003","Ibn Jurayj reported, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that an old man of the people of Sham informed him, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, that he buried a woman of the People of the Book pregnant from a Muslim in the graveyard of the Muslims."
"10004","Ibn Jurayj reported from Sulayman ibn Musa that Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' buried a Christian woman who died pregnant from a Muslim in a graveyard neither the graveyard of the Muslims nor the graveyard of the Christians, between that. Sulayman said: And the people of her religion take charge of her."
"10005","Ibn Jurayj reported from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Muraqqa' ibn Sayfi, he testified upon his grandfather Rabah ibn Rabi' al-Hanzali, that he informed him: He went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a campaign he campaigned; Khalid ibn al-Walid was over the vanguard. Rabah and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a slain woman of what the vanguard had struck; they stood over her looking, marvelling at her creation, until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came upon a camel of his. They made way from the woman, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood looking at her and said: She was not one to fight. Then he looked at the faces of the people; he said to one of them: Join Khalid and say: Do not kill offspring nor a hireling."
"10006","Abu Said Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad ibn Bishr informed us he said: Abu Yaqub Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abbad al-Dabari narrated to us he said: We read to Abd al-Razzaq ibn Hammam from Ibn Jurayj from Ata he said: Whoever marries in jest or divorces it has taken effect and he said: There is no jesting in divorce and marriage."
"10007","From Ibn Jurayj he said: Abd al-Karim informed me that Ibn Masud said: Whoever divorces in jest or marries in jest it has taken effect."
"10008","From Mamar from Qatada from al-Hasan from Abu al-Darda he said: Three in which jest is like seriousness: marriage divorce and emancipation. From Abdullah from Qatada from al-Hasan from Abu al-Darda the like of it."
"10009","From al-Thawri from Jabir from Abdullah ibn Nujayy from Ali he said: Three there is no jesting in them: marriage divorce emancipation and charity. He said: And one of the three qualities is not in the hadith: marriage or divorce or emancipation I do not know which of them it is."
"10010","From Ibrahim ibn Umar from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayya from Jada ibn Hubayra that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Three in which the jester and the serious are equal: divorce charity and emancipation. Abd al-Karim said: And Talq ibn Habib said: And sacrificial offering and vow."
"10011","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad from Safwan ibn Sulaym that Abu Dharr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever divorces while jesting his divorce is valid and whoever emancipates while jesting his emancipation is valid and whoever marries while jesting his marriage is valid."
"10012","From Ibn Jurayj he said: I was informed from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever divorces or marries in jest it has taken effect."
"10013","From Ibn Uyayna from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam he said: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyib mention from Marwan he said: A matter in which there is no reversal except through marriage divorce emancipation and vow. Ibn Uyayna said: And it reached me that Marwan took them from Ali ibn Abi Talib."
"10014","From Ibn Jurayj and al-Thawri from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyib he said: I heard him say: Three there is no jesting in them: marriage divorce and emancipation."
"10015","From Ibn Jurayj he said: No marriage divorce or taking back is valid except with two witnesses and if he takes back and neglects to have witnesses while he visits her and has intercourse with her then when he learns let him return to the Sunna by having two just witnesses bear witness."
"10016","From Mamar from Ayyub from Ibn Sirin he said: A man asked Imran ibn Husayn about a man who divorced without witnesses and took back without witnesses he said: He divorced outside the waiting-period manner and took back outside the Sunna so let him have witnesses to his divorce and to his return and let him seek Allahs forgiveness. Mamar said: And Qatada narrated to me from al-Ala ibn Ziyad from Imran ibn al-Husayn the like of that."
"10017","From Ibn Jurayj he said: Ayyub ibn Abi Tamima informed me from Ibn Sirin that a man asked Imran ibn al-Husayn and said: A man divorced without witnesses and took back without witnesses he said: Evil is what he did he divorced in innovation and took back outside the Sunna let him have witnesses to what he did."
"10018","From al-Thawri from Yunus ibn Ubayd from Ibn Sirin from Imran ibn al-Husayn he said: A man asked him and said: I divorced without witnesses and I took back without witnesses so he said: You divorced outside the waiting-period manner and took back outside the Sunna."
"10019","From Mamar from al-Zuhri he said: If he has intercourse then his entering upon her is a return but let him have witnesses."
"10020","From Mamar and one who heard al-Hakam ibn Utayba informed me he says: His entering upon her is a return."
"10021","From al-Thawri from Mughira from Ibrahim he said: If he has intercourse then his entering upon her is a return. Al-Thawri said: And Jabir informed me from al-Shabi the like of it."
"10022","From Ibn Jurayj from Ata he said: His entering upon her is a return but let him have witnesses when he learns so that he returns to the Sunna."
"10023","From al-Thawri from Sulayman al-Taymi from Tawus he said: His entering upon her is a return but let him have witnesses and al-Thawri said: If he kisses her it is a return."
"10024","From Mamar he said: I heard Ayyub asking Matar al-Warraq about a man who said: My wife is divorced if she enters the house of so-and-so then she entered while he did not know and he continued to have intercourse with her while he did not know. Matar said: Al-Hasan and Ibn al-Musayyib used to say: His having intercourse with her is a return but let him have witnesses. Mamar said: And al-Zuhri said it."
"10025","From Mamar from al-Zuhri he said: If he does not have witnesses to the return until the waiting period ends then he claims the return after the end of the waiting period he is not believed and even if he brings witnesses to that he is not believed."
"10026","From al-Thawri from Mughira from al-Thawri he said: If he divorces one or two divorces then claims the return he said: He is asked for proof that he has returned and al-Thawri holds by this."
"10027","From Mamar from al-Zuhri: About a man who divorced his wife until when the waiting period ended he said: I had returned her during her waiting period and the woman denied that he said: The woman is made to swear and he is not believed against her and she has more right to herself and if they agree she is his wife."
"10028","From al-Thawri: About a man who divorced his wife once then she remained three years then she gave birth and he said: I had taken you back and she said: You did not take me back with a return because the child could only be from intercourse after the divorce and intercourse is a return. He said: If that was two years or less than that he is asked for proof of the return otherwise the child is attached to him and she is separated from him because the child can be at two years."
"10029","From Ibn Jurayj from Amr ibn Shuayb he said: Allah and His Messenger decreed concerning witnesses: four for zina so whoever less than four testifies to zina they are lashed and if four testify against two married persons they are both stoned and if they testify against two virgins they are both lashed as Allah said: one hundred lashes and let no pity for them take you in Allahs religion and they are exiled for a year to other than the land they were in and their exile is separate and if they testify against a virgin and a married person the virgin is lashed and the married is stoned so the testimony of three nor two nor one is accepted and they are lashed eighty eighty and their testimony is not accepted until clear repentance and reform appears from them to the Muslims and for divorce two witnesses and for marriage two witnesses and for wine two witnesses then its drinker is lashed and frightened and harmed until repentance appears from him and the testimony of one witness is not valid for divorce nor marriage so whoever divorces and one witness testifies against him and he denies then he is made to swear by Allah: I did not divorce and if he swears she is his wife and if he refuses she is divorced by what the witness testified and he is the other witness when he refuses and nothing is valid for a due right except two witnesses then his right is enforced for him and if one just witness testifies the owner of the right is made to swear with a witness if he is just and if it is a claim with no witness in it then the defendant has more right to the oath than the word of the claimant and if he refuses the owner of the right deserves his oath and the testimony of a treacherous man nor treacherous woman nor adversary who harbors enmity against his fellow is not valid and Allah commanded two just ones from the witnesses and He said: Those who purchase with Allahs covenant and their oaths a small price the verse so let a man consider upon what he testified."
"10030","From Mamar from Ayyub from Ibn Sirin he said: Al-Ashath ibn Qays went out escorting a man I think him from Quraysh and he saw his wife or a woman with him and she pleased him then it was decreed that the man died on his journey and his family returned to Kufa and al-Ashath proposed to that woman and she said: Will you marry me on my terms so he married her and when he consummated with her and remained what he remained he divorced her then he said: Decide whatever you wish and she said: I decide so-and-so and so-and-so slaves of his father and he said: As for these then no but decide from my wealth so he disputed with her to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: O Commander of the Faithful I fell in love with this woman and he said: That is as long as you did not possess. He said: Then I married her on her terms then I divorced her before I pleased her so Umar rejected that and said: A woman from the Muslims she has what a woman from the Muslims has and he did not grant her terms and he granted her the dower of a woman like her from her women. From Hisham ibn Muhammad the like of it."
"10031","From al-Hasan ibn Umara from al-Hakam ibn Utayba that Ali said: About a man who marries a woman on her terms he said: The marriage is valid and she has the dower of her likes neither deficient nor excessive. Al-Hasan said: And al-Hakam informed me from Shurayh and Ibrahim the like of it."
"10032","From Ibn Jurayj from Ata he said: I said to him: A man married a woman and delegated to him then before he consummated with her he was charged with her dower and it was said to him: Assign for her the like of the dower of her likes he said: That is not for them it is only what her husband wishes. I said: So he sent to her something absolving himself with it then he entered upon her and had intercourse with her then he died or divorced her and he had not named her dower he said: They have nothing except what they agree upon by will. I said: So he died and did not name a dower and he had had intercourse with her he said: She has nothing except inheritance and what the heir wishes."
"10033","From Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Shihab he said: If he enters upon her before he assigns for her then the like of the dower of her women is due."
"10034","From Mamar from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from al-Muhajir ibn Ikrima he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to consult his daughters when he married them he said: He would sit at the chamber of the betrothed and say: So-and-so mentions so-and-so and if she moved the chamber he would not marry her and if she was silent he married her. From al-Thawri from Hisham Sahib al-Dastuwai from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from al-Muhajir ibn Ikrima."
"10035","Umar ibn Rashid informed us from Yahya from al-Muhajir: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when one of his daughters was proposed to would come to the chamber and say: So-and-so proposes to so-and-so and if she moved the chamber he would not marry her and if she was silent he married her."
"10036","From al-Thawri from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari from Ibn al-Musayyib he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Consult virgins about themselves for they are shy and if she is silent it is her consent."
"10037","From Mamar from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari from Ibn al-Musayyib he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give women authority over themselves."
"10038","From al-Thawri from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim from Ibn Abbas he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The previously married woman has more right to herself than her guardian and the virgin is asked permission. From Malik that Abdullah ibn al-Fadl narrated to him from Nafi from Ibn Abbas the like of it."
"10039","From Ibn Jurayj he said: Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman informed me that a man narrated to him from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl from Nafi ibn Jubayr he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The previously married woman owns her affair and the virgin is consulted about herself and her silence is her acknowledgment."
"10040","From Ibn Jurayj he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulayka say: Dhakwan freedman of Aisha said she says: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the young girl whom her family marries is she consulted or not so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Yes she is consulted. Aisha said: So I said: She is shy and remains silent so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is her permission when she is silent."
"10041","From Mamar from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The previously married woman is consulted and the virgin is asked permission. They said: And what is her permission O Prophet of Allah He said: That she be silent."
"10042","From Ibn Jurayj he said: I said to Ata: Are women consulted about their private affairs the previously married and the virgin He said: Yes I said: And does the father consult He said: Yes."
"10043","From Ibn Jurayj he said: Ibn Tawus informed me from his father he said: I heard him say: Women are consulted about their private affairs. He said: And Ibn Tawus said to me: Except ... men in that are like daughters they are not coerced and more strongly so."
"10044","From Ibn Jurayj from Ata al-Khurasani: That Zaynab daughter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was married in the Jahiliyya and Ali and Uthman married in Islam and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to the chamber of the betrothed from his daughters and say: So-and-so proposes to so-and-so and if she struck her hand on her chamber that is refusal from her so he would not marry her and if she did not strike her hand on her chamber the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her and was silent. Ibn Jurayj said: And I was informed from Ikrima freedman of Ibn Abbas something like this hadith."
"10045","From Mamar from Habib from Nafi he said: Ibn Umar used to consult his daughters about their marriage."
"10046","From al-Thawri from Asim from al-Shabi he said: The father consults the virgin and the previously married."
"10047","From al-Thawri from Mansur from Ibrahim he said: As for the virgin her father does not consult her and as for the previously married if she is in his household he does not consult her and if she is not in his household he consults her."
"10048","From Ibn Jurayj from Ata he said: The marriage of the father over the virgin is valid and it is not valid over the previously married."
"10049","From Mamar from al-Zuhri from Ibn al-Musayyib he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The orphan girl is consulted about herself and her silence is her acknowledgment."
"10050","From Mamar from Ayyub from Ibn Sirin he said: The orphan girl is consulted and her silence is her consent."
"10051","From al-Thawri from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqama from Abu Salama from Abu Hurayra that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The orphan girl is consulted about herself and if she is silent it is her consent."
"10052","From al-Thawri from Mansur from Ibrahim he said: Umar wrote that the orphan girl is consulted about herself and if she is silent it is her consent. He said: And al-Shabi said: If she is silent or weeps or laughs it is her consent and if she refuses it is not valid over her."
"10053","From Mamar from Salih ibn Kaysan from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The guardian has no authority along with the previously married woman and the orphan girl is consulted and her silence is her acknowledgment."
"10054","From Mamar from al-Hasan and al-Zuhri they said: The order of the father is valid over the virgin in marriage if he is not foolish."
"10055","From Mamar from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Muhajir ibn Ikrima that a virgin whom her father married while she disliked it her father brought her to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so he returned her affair to her."
"10056","From Jafar ibn Sulayman he said: Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to me that Abdullah ibn Burayda narrated to him he said: A virgin woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah my father married me to a son of a brother of his to raise his lowliness through me and he did not consult me so do I have any authority over myself So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. And she said: I would not reject anything my father did but I loved that women know whether they have authority over themselves or not."
"10057","From Israil ibn Yunus from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rafi from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman he said: A woman wanted to marry the paternal uncle of her sons but her father married her to other than him and he did not fall short of good so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him and said: I wanted to marry the uncle of my child so I would be with my child and I disliked being without a husband so he married me to other than him and he did not fall short of good so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to her father and said: Did you marry her while she disliked He said: Yes. He said: Go you have no marriage contract go and marry whomever you wish."
"10058","Ibn Jurayj informed us he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me from a righteous man from the people of Medina from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman he said: There was a woman from the Ansar under a man from the Ansar and he was killed leaving her on the day of Uhud and he had a child from her and the uncle of her child proposed to her and a man to her father so he married her to the man and left the uncle of her child so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father married me to a man I do not want and left the uncle of my child so my child will be taken from me so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called her father and said: Did you marry so-and-so to so-and-so He said: Yes He said: You are the one who has no marriage contract go and marry the uncle of your child."
"10059","From Mamar from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salama and Ayyub from Ikrima: That a previously married woman whom her father married came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father married me while I disliked so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put her affair to her."
"10060","From Ibn Jurayj he said: Ayyub informed me from Ikrima and from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir that a previously married woman and a virgin whom their father married came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father married me so he annulled their marriage."
"10061","From al-Thawri from Abu al-Huwayrith from Nafi ibn Jubayr he said: Khansa daughter of Khidham became husbandless and her father married her while she disliked so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father married me while I disliked and he did not inform me and I have taken control of my affair. He said: He has no marriage contract marry whomever you wish so he annulled his marriage and she married Abu Lubaba al-Ansari."
"10062","From Ibn Jurayj he said: Ata al-Khurasani informed me from Ibn Abbas that Khidham Abu Wadia married his daughter to a man so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained to him that she was married while she disliked so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took her away from her husband and said: Do not coerce them. And she married after that Abu Lubaba al-Ansari and she was previously married. He said: I was informed that she is Khansa daughter of Khidham from the people of Quba Ibn Jurayj is the speaker."
"10063","From Mamar from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jahshi from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad: That a man from the Ansar called Unays ibn Qatada was married to Khansa daughter of Khidham and he was killed leaving her on the day of Uhud so her father married her to a man and she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father married me to a man and the uncle of my child is more beloved to me than him so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put her affair to her."
"10064","From Ibn Jurayj he said: Ismail ibn Umayya informed me from more than one from the people of Medina: That Nuaym ibn Abdullah had a daughter and Abdullah ibn Umar proposed to her and named for her a large dower so Nuaym married her to an orphan of his from Banu Adi ibn Kab who had no wealth and her mother went and mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Abdullah had mentioned her daughter and had named for her much wealth so her father married her to an orphan who has no wealth and left Abdullah and he had named for her much wealth so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and mentioned to him and he said: Yes I married her to my orphan and he is more deserving than one whose orphanhood I lifted and whom I joined and he said: She has from my wealth the like of what Abdullah named for her so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give women authority over their daughters."
"10065","From al-Thawri from Ismail ibn Umayya he said: The trustworthy or one I do not suspect informed me from Ibn Umar that he proposed to a relative of his his daughter and the inclination of the womans mother was toward Ibn Umar and the inclination of her father was toward an orphan of his. He said: So the father married her to that orphan of his and she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give women authority over their daughters."
"10066","From Mamar he said: It reached me that the orphan girl her brother does not coerce her to marriage even if he is upright."
"10067","From Ibn Jurayj he said: I said to Ata: Is the marriage of a man over his daughter a virgin while she dislikes valid He said: Yes I said: And a previously married disliking He said: No the previously married owns her affair it is not valid over her. He said: And more beloved to me if the father of the virgin calls the virgin to a man and she calls to another even if the one her father called to is higher in position and dower when the one she called to has no harm her desire is not followed I fear there is something in her mind about him and if her father overcomes her he has more right to that."
"10068","From Ibn Jurayj from Ata he said: We heard that the affair of the orphan girl is to her and the marriage of her brother over her is not valid except with her permission."
"10069","From Ibn Jurayj he said: Ibn Tawus informed me from his father he said: About the previously married she is not coerced to marry one she dislikes. I said: She desired a desire and her father desired a desire He said: He used to like that she be joined to her desire."
"10070","From Mamar and others from Yahya ibn Said from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad that a woman from Banu Amr ibn Awf whom her father married while she disliked came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so he annulled her marriage except with her permission and she was previously married."
"10071","From Ibn Jurayj and Mamar from Ayyub ibn Abi Tamima from Ibn Sirin: A woman became husbandless in Medina and Umar met her guardian and said: Mention me to her and when he was slow upon him he entered upon her and with her was her guardian. He said: I do not know did he mention this to you anything She said: Yes and I have no need of you nor of what he mentioned but order him to marry me to so-and-so. And her guardian said: No by Allah I will not do it. And Umar said: Why He said: Because you mentioned her and so-and-so and so-and-so mentioned her and I do not know a noble left in Medina until he mentioned her and she refused except so-and-so. And Umar said: I adjure you to marry her to him if you do not know a defect in his religion. From Mamar from Ayyub from Ibn Sirin the like of it."
"10072","From Mamar from Ibrahim ibn Maysara he said: A young man proposed to a woman who had loved him but they refused to marry her to him so I asked Tawus and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing has been seen for two who love like marriage and he ordered me to marry."
"10073","From Ibn Jurayj he said: Amr informed me from Ikrima that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not burden women with what they dislike."
"10074","From al-Thawri from Yunus ibn Ubayd from Ibn Sirin he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: There is nothing in me from the affair of Jahiliyya except two things: except that I do not care which of the Muslims I marry nor which of them I marry."
"10075","From Ibn Jurayj he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Bakr informed me that Umar ibn al-Khattab used to be strict about equals."
"10076","From Ibn Jurayj from Muhammad ibn Qays from Habib ibn Abi Thabit that Umar said: If it is a year of drought the people of the desert have no marriage."
"10077","From al-Thawri from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talha he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: I shall surely prevent the private parts of women of lineage except from equals."
"10078","From Mamar from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there comes to you one whose trustworthiness and character you approve then marry him whoever he be and if you do not do there will be tribulation in the land and great corruption or he said: wide."
"10079","From al-Thawri from Jabir from al-Shabi he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I married al-Miqdad and Zayd so that your noblest before Allah be your best in Islam. Al-Miqdad married Dubaa daughter of al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib and he married Zayd ibn Haritha to Zaynab daughter of Jahsh and al-Miqdad had been afflicted by captivity."
"10080","From Ibn Jurayj he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr mention that a woman from Banu Bakr ibn Kinana married a freedman in Iraq and they differed about him so they referred that to Ubayd ibn Umayr and he validated his marriage."
"10081","From Ibn Jurayj he said: I was narrated that Salman al-Farisi married a previously married woman from Kinda."
"10082","From Israil from Abu Ishaq from Abu Layla al-Kindi he said: Salman came with twelve men from the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and prayer came and they said: Advance O Abu Abdullah and he said: We neither lead you nor marry your women Allah has guided us through you. He said: Then a man from the people advanced while he was a traveler and prayed four with them and when he finished Salman said: What have we to do with four indeed half of four suffices us we are more in need of the concession."
"10083","From al-Thawri he said: If a man comes to a people and says: I am an Arab and marries among them and they find him a freedman they have to annul his marriage and if he says: I am a freedman and they find him a Nabatean the marriage is annulled and if he says: I am an Arab and he is an Arab from other than those he ascribed himself to the marriage is valid and if he says: I am a freedman of Banu so-and-so and they find him a freedman of others the marriage is valid. Abd al-Razzaq said: And he used to hold separation if a freedman married an Arab woman and was strict about it."
"10084","From Ibn Jurayj he said: And Ibn Shihab claimed that Umar ibn al-Khattab said on the pulpit: By the One in whose hand is Umars soul I shall surely prevent the private parts of women of lineage except from people of lineage for the bedouins when there is drought have no marriage for them. And he mentioned something to them and Bilal married Fatima daughter of Utba ibn Rabia and after her he married a daughter of Utba ibn al-Walid ibn Rabia a maternal aunt from the Ansar and Abu Hudhayfa adopted him as the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) adopted Zayd until was revealed: Call them by their fathers."
"10085","From Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa from Aisha that Abu Hudhayfa ibn Rabia and he was a Badr veteran married Salim freedman of Abu Hudhayfa to Fatima daughter of al-Walid ibn Utba and Salim is freedman of a woman from the Ansar."
"10086","Mamar informed us from Thabit al-Bunani from Anas he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed on behalf of Julaybib a woman from the Ansar to her father and he said: Until I consult her mother so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes then. So the man went to his wife and mentioned that to her and she said: No by Allah then what did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) find except Julaybib and we have refused her to so-and-so and so-and-so. He said: And the girl was in her cover hearing. He said: So the man set out wanting to inform the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the girl said: Do you want to reject the order of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) If he is pleased with him for you then marry him to her so it was as if she released them from her parents and she said: You spoke truth so her father went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: If you are pleased with him then I am pleased with him. He said: So he married her then the people of Medina were alarmed and Julaybib rode and they found him killed and found around him people from the polytheists he had killed. Anas said: I saw her and she was the most spending daughter in Medina."
"10087","From Ibn Jurayj he said: I was informed that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Bring out the young girl who has not reached puberty so that her cousins may desire her."
"10088","From al-Thawri from Asim al-Ahwal from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani and I am Mamar from Thabit al-Bunani from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani that al-Mughira ibn Shuba said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned to him a woman I was proposing so he said: Go and look at her for it is more likely to create affection between you. He said: So I came to a woman from the Ansar and proposed her to her parents and informed them of the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and it was as if they disliked that and I heard that woman saying: If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered you to look then look otherwise I adjure you as if she deemed that great. He said: So I looked at her and married her and he mentioned her compatibility."
"10089","From Mamar from Ibn Tawus from his father that he said to him about a woman he wanted to marry: Go and look at her. He said: So I dressed my clothes and oiled and prepared and when he saw me do that he said: Sit he disliked that I go to her in that state."
"10090","From Yahya ibn al-Ala from Dawud ibn al-Husayn from Waqid ibn Amr ibn Sad ibn Muadh from Jabir ibn Abdullah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no sin upon one of you when he wants to propose a woman to deceive her in looking that he looks at her if he is pleased he marries and if displeased he leaves."
"10091","From Yahya ibn al-Ala from al-Hajjaj ibn Artat from Muhammad ibn Sulayman from Sahl ibn Abi Hathma he said: People from the Ansar passed by Muhammad ibn Maslama while he was peering at a girl from Banu al-Najjar and they said: Glory be to Allah if some of our youths did this we would see it ugly. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah casts in the heart of a man proposal of a woman there is no harm that he looks at her."
"10092","From al-Thawri from Hisham from Urwa that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: One of you goes to his daughter and marries her to the ugly indeed they love what you love meaning: when he marries her to the hideous she dislikes in that what he dislikes and disobeys Allah in it."
"10093","From Ibn Jurayj he said: I was narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim and other than him entered my mind that Aisha used to call the sons of her brother and place between them and the sons of her brother a garment she seeing them from behind it and wherever a girl inclined to a youth she married her to him and when she wanted to marry him to her she called a group from her family and testified until when marriage contracting remained she said: Contract O so-and-so for women do not contract marriages."
"10094","From Mamar from Ibn Khuthaym from Makhul he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is virgins so marry them for they have more open wombs and sweeter mouths and more youthful freshness."
"10095","From Ibn Jurayj he said: I was narrated from Makhul he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Marry young virgin girls for they have sweetest mouths and cleanest wombs and most youthful character did you not know that I compete with you in numbers and that the offspring of the believers are in a tree from the trees of Paradise their father Ibrahim (peace be upon him) cares for them."
"10096","Ibn Jurayj said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Marry young virgin girls for they have sweetest mouths and sweeter and more open wombs."
"10097","From Hisham ibn Hassan from Muhammad ibn Sirin he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave the beautiful barren and marry the black fertile for I compete with you in nations on the Day of Resurrection even the miscarried remains angry that is resentful and it is said to him: Enter Paradise and he says: Until my parents enter and it is said: Enter you and your parents."
"10098","From Mamar from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr and Asim Ibn Bahdala that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: A daughter of an uncle of mine with beauty and wealth and she is barren shall I marry her So he forbade him from her twice or thrice then he said: A black fertile woman is more beloved to me than her did you not know that I compete with you in nations and that the children of the Muslim nations it is said to them on the Day of Resurrection: Enter Paradise and they cling to the waists of their fathers and mothers and say: Our Lord our fathers and our mothers. He said: So it is said to them: Enter Paradise you and your fathers and your mothers. He said: Then the miscarried comes and it is said to him: Enter Paradise. He said: So he remains withholding that is holding back he says: O Lord my father and my mother until his father joins him. Abd al-Razzaq said: I was informed that a man said: O Prophet of Allah I have a daughter of an uncle barren and I wanted to marry her. He said: Do not marry her then he returned the second and third in different sittings and each time the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: Do not marry her then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That you marry a black fertile is better than that you marry her beautiful comely who does not bear."
"10099","From Mamar and Ibn Jurayj from Ayyub from Ibn Sirin he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab sent a man over alms collection and he came to him and said: I married a woman and he said: Did you inform her that you are sterile no child is born to you He said: No. He said: Inform her and give her choice. From Hisham ibn Hassan from Muhammad ibn Sirin the like of it from al-Thawri from Khalid from Ibn Sirin the like of it."
"10100","From Mamar from al-Zuhri from Urwa he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Aisha when she was six and she was presented to him when she was nine and her toys with her and he died leaving her when she was eighteen. From Mamar from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father the like of it."
"10101","From Mamar from Ayyub and others from Ikrima that Ali ibn Abi Talib married his daughter a girl playing with girls to Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"10102","From Ibn Uyayna from Amr ibn Dinar from Abu Jafar he said: Umar proposed to Ali his daughter and he said: She is small and it was said to Umar: He only means by that preventing her. He said: Speak to him and Ali said: I will send her to you and if you are pleased she is your wife. He said: So he sent her to him. He said: So Umar went and uncovered her leg and she said: Send away for were you not Commander of the Faithful I would have struck your neck."
"10103","From Ibn Jurayj he said: I heard al-Amash say: Umar ibn al-Khattab proposed to Ali his daughter and he said: What is with you except preventing her. He said: I shall send her and if you are pleased she is your wife and I have married you and he adorned her and sent her to him and he said: I am pleased and he took her leg and she said: By Allah were you not Commander of the Faithful I would have struck your eye."
"10104","From Mamar from Ayyub from Ikrima he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab married Umm Kulthum daughter of Ali ibn Abi Talib while she was a girl playing with girls and he came to his companions and they prayed for blessing for him and he said: I did not marry from liveliness in me but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every cause and lineage is cut off on the Day of Resurrection except my cause and my lineage so I loved that there be between me and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cause and lineage. Abd al-Razzaq said: And Umm Kulthum is from Fatima daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Umar entered upon her and fathered from her a boy called Zayd and it reached me that Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan poisoned them and they died and Abdullah ibn Umar prayed over them and that is because it was said to Abd al-Malik: This is the son of Ali and the son of Umar and he feared for his kingdom so he poisoned them."
"10105","From Mamar from al-Hasan and al-Zuhri and Qatada they said: If their fathers marry minors their marriage is valid. Abd al-Razzaq said: And by this we take."
"10106","From al-Thawri from Jabir from al-Shabi he said: None compels to marriage except the father."
"10107","From Mamar from Ibn Tawus from his father he said: If their father marries two minors they have choice when they grow."
"10108","From Mamar from al-Zuhri that Urwa ibn al-Zubayr married his son small to a daughter of Musab small."
"10109","From al-Thawri from Hisham ibn Urwa he said: My father married his son small this one five years and this one six and he died and she inherited four thousand dinars or about that."
"10110","From Ibn Jurayj from Ata he said: I heard that the affair of the orphan girl is to her the marriage of her brother is not valid except with her permission."
"10111","From al-Thawri from Jabir from al-Shabi he said: None compels to marriage except the father."
"10112","From Mamar from Ibn Tawus from his father he said: If the orphan boy and the orphan girl are married while they are small they have choice when they grow. Abd al-Razzaq said: And by this we take."
"10113","From Ibn Jurayj from Ata he said: If an orphan boy is married small he has choice when he grows and the orphan girl likewise."
"10114","From Mamar from Qatada he said: If their guardian marries two children and they die before they reach puberty there is no inheritance between them. And al-Thawri said it."
"10115","From Mamar from Ibn Tawus from his father he said: If their guardian marries two children before they reach puberty there is no inheritance between them."
"10116","From Mamar from Qatada he said: If two minors one his father married and the other his guardian married and the one his father married dies the other inherits him and if the one his guardian married dies the other does not inherit him. Mamar said: What he said did not please me there is no inheritance between them."
"10117","From al-Thawri from Ibn Shubruma he said: Two minors have choice when they reach."
"10118","From Mamar from Ibn Tawus from his father he said: They have choice when they reach."
"10119","From Mamar from al-Zuhri he said: If a guardian marries a boy and he does not fear himself or others leaving if it was a consideration looking out for him."
"10120","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr and Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote to an agent of his: If the orphan boy and the orphan girl are married while they are small they have choice when they reach."
"10121","From Mamar he said: We heard that the orphan girl her brother does not coerce her even if he is upright."
"10122","From Mamar from Qatada: About a man who married his son small who has no wealth then the boy died he said: There is no dower upon his son if the boy had no wealth except that the father bore the dower."
"10123","From al-Thawri he said: The father is not held for the dower of his son if he was married and died small except that the father guaranteed something."
"10124","From al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah that Amr ibn Shuayb informed him from Said ibn al-Musayyib that a group from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among them Ali ibn Abi Talib and Abdullah ibn Amr when they devoted themselves and sat in houses and withdrew from women and intended castration and resolved night prayer and day fasting that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so he called them and said: As for me I pray and sleep and fast and break fast and marry women so whoever turns away from my Sunna is not from me."
"10125","From Mamar from al-Zuhri from Urwa and Amra from Aisha she said: The wife of Uthman ibn Mazun named Khawla daughter of Hakim entered upon Aisha while she was unkempt in appearance and she asked her: What is your matter And she said: My husband stands the night and fasts the day so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and Aisha mentioned that to him and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met him and said: O Uthman monasticism was not written upon us do you not have in me an example By Allah I am the most fearing of Allah among you and most preserving of His limits."
"10126","Al-Zuhri said and Ibn al-Musayyib informed me he said: I heard Sad ibn Abi Waqqas say: He rejected meaning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for Uthman ibn Mazun celibacy and had he permitted it for him we would have castrated."
"10127","From Ibn Jurayj he said: Abu al-Mughallis informed me that Abu Najih informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is able to marry then does not marry is not from me."
"10128","Ibn Jurayj and Mamar informed us from Ibrahim ibn Maysara that he heard Tawus say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have not seen for two who love like marriage."
"10129","From Ibn Jurayj he said: Ibrahim ibn Maysara informed me that he heard Ubayd ibn Sad say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves my nature let him follow my Sunna and from my Sunna is marriage."
"10130","From Mamar from Ayyub that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever follows my Sunna is from me and from my Sunna is marriage."
"10131","From al-Thawri from al-Amash from Umara ibn Umayr from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid from Abdullah ibn Masud he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of youths whoever among you is able to bear the cost let him marry for it lowers the gaze and guards the private part and whoever is not able upon him is fasting for it is a restraint for him. Mamar said: And al-Amash informed me from Umara from Abd al-Rahman from Abdullah the like of it."
"10132","From Ibn Jurayj he said: I was informed that Ibn Masud performed Hajj and saw Uthman in al-Khayf and called him then they saw Alqama and called him and Ibn Masud said: O Commander of the Faithful inform Alqama: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say when he passed by youths He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he passed by youths and said: Whoever among you has means let him marry for it lowers the gaze and guards the private part and whoever does not let him fast for fasting is a restraint for him."
"10133","From Mamar from Abu Ishaq he said: I entered upon him and he said to me: Have you gathered the Quran He said: I said: Yes and praise be to Allah. He said: Have you performed Hajj He said: I said: Yes. He said: Have you married He said: I said: No. He said: What prevents you And Abdullah ibn Masud said: Were only one day left of the world I would love to have a wife in it."
"10134","From Mamar from Ibn Tawus from his father Umar said to a man: Have you married He said: No. He said: Either you are foolish or you are immoral."
"10135","From Ibn Uyayna from Ibrahim ibn Maysara he said: Tawus said to me: You shall surely marry or I shall say to you what Umar said to Abu al-Zawaid: Nothing prevents you from marriage except incapacity or immorality."
"10136","Hisham ibn Hassan informed us from al-Hasan he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Seek bounty in marriage. He said: And Umar recited: If they are poor Allah will enrich them from His bounty."
"10137","From al-Mundhir he said: I heard Wahb ibn Munabbih say: The likeness of the bachelor is like a tree in a desert the winds turn it thus and thus."
"10138","From Muhammad ibn Rashid he said: I heard Makhul narrate from a man from Abu Dharr he said: A man called Akkaf ibn Bishr al-Tamimi entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you have a wife He said: No. He said: Nor a concubine He said: Nor a concubine. He said: And you are well-off with good He said: And I am well-off with good. He said: You are then from the brothers of the devils had you been from the Christians you would have been from their monks indeed from our Sunna is marriage your worst are your bachelors and the vilest of your dead are your bachelors by the devils you wrestle the devils have no weapon more effective against the righteous than women except the married those are the purified cleared of indecency. Woe to you O Akkaf they are the companions of Ayyub and Dawud and Kursuf and Yusuf. And Bishr ibn Atiyya said to him: And who is Kursuf O Messenger of Allah He said: A man who worshipped Allah on a coast from the coasts of the sea three hundred years fasting the day and standing the night then he disbelieved in Allah the Mighty in the cause of a woman he loved and left what he was upon of worship of his Lord then Allah remedied him with some of what was from him and turned to him. Woe to you O Akkaf marry otherwise you are from the wavering. He said: Marry me O Messenger of Allah. He said: So he married him to Karima daughter of Kulthum al-Himyari."
"10139","From Ibn Uyayna from Amr ibn Dinar he said: Ibn Umar wanted not to marry after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Hafsa said: O my brother marry for if a child is born to you and dies he will be a forerunner for you and if he remains he will pray for you with good."
"10140","From Ibn Uyayna from a man among them called Nusayba he said: When Yusuf met his brother he said to him: Did you marry after me He said: Yes. He said: And did grief over me not distract you He said: Your father Yaqub said to me: Marry perhaps Allah will produce from you offspring who burden or he said: inhabit the earth with glorification."
"10141","From Yahya ibn al-Ala from al-Hajjaj ibn Artat from Makhul from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Circumcision siwak perfuming and marriage are from my Sunna."
"10142","From Ibn Jurayj he said: I was informed from Hisham ibn Sad from Said ibn Abi Hilal that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Marry and multiply for I boast with you over the nations on the Day of Resurrection. A man marries a young beautiful woman from the protected non-Muslims and when she grows old he divorces her. Fear Allah concerning women indeed from the right of the woman upon her husband is that he feeds her and clothes her and if she commits indecency he strikes her a strike not severe."
"10143","Ibn Jurayj informed us he said: I was informed that those who passed used to order their youths to lengthen their hair for that diminishes that."
"10144","From Mamar from Qatada that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: I have not seen the like of a man who does not seek bounty in marriage and Allah says: If they are poor Allah will enrich them from His bounty."
"10145","From Ibn Jurayj he said: I said to Ata: I sent to them my sandals and they were pleased with them. He said: And what do they do with your sandals He said: And it is said: The least that suffices is his ring or a garment he sends with it."
"10146","From Ibn Jurayj from Amr ibn Dinar and Abd al-Karim they said: The least dower is what they agree upon. Abd al-Karim said: And they say: There was gold not reaching a dinar."
"10147","Ibn Jurayj informed us he said: Ibn Abi al-Husayn narrated to me that he heard Ikrima say: Ali made Fatima lawful to himself only with a body of iron. Amr said: He did not increase her over it. From Ibn Uyayna from Amr the like of it."
"10148","Ibn Jurayj informed us he said: Ibn Abi al-Husayn narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be easy in dower indeed a man gives the woman until that remains in himself against her as rancor and until he says: I did not come to you until I drove to you the strap of the water-skin."
"10149","From Mamar from Ayyub from Ibn Sirin from Abu al-Ajfa that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Do not be excessive in dowers of women for had it been honor in the world and piety before Allah the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have been most deserving of it among you. No woman from his wives nor from his daughters was given more than twelve uqiyya and a man is excessive with the woman in her dower and it becomes regret in his chest and he says: I burdened myself to you the strap of the water-skin. He said: I was a young slave born and I did not know what this is He said: And another they say for one killed in these your raids: So-and-so was killed a martyr or so-and-so died a martyr and perhaps he went out having loaded or tied behind his mount or its rear paper seeking trade but say as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed in Allahs path or dies then for him is Paradise. From al-Thawri from Asim from Ibn Sirin from Abu al-Ajfa from Umar the like of it. Al-Thawri said: And his saying: I burdened myself to you the strap of the water-skin he says: I hung the water-skin in the deserts to you fearing thirst meaning the worn-out skin."
"10150","From Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad from Nafi he said Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Do not be excessive in dowers of women for had it been piety for Him the daughters of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have been most deserving of it among you. He did not marry nor marry off except upon twelve uqiyya."
"10151","Nafi' said: Umar used to say: The dowries of women should not exceed four hundred dirhams, except what they mutually agree upon below that. Nafi' said: A man from the descendants of Umar married off his daughter for six hundred dirhams. He said: Had he known of that, he would have punished him. He said: And when he forbade something, he would say to his household: I have forbidden such-and-such, and people look at you as kites look at meat, so beware of it."
"10152","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad reported from Safwan ibn Sulaym that Ali gave Fatima, daughter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a dower of twelve uqiyyas."
"10153","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Ali ibn Yahya, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of your women are not those with the highest dower; had that been superiority, the daughters of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have been most entitled to it."
"10154","From Dawud ibn Qays, from Zayd ibn Aslam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never gave to any of his wives, nor was given for any of his daughters, more than twelve uqiyyas; that is four hundred and eighty dirhams."
"10155","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, who said: The dower of every wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was twelve uqiyyas of gold; that is four hundred and eighty dirhams."
"10156","From Dawud ibn Qays, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Our dower, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us, was ten uqiyyas, four hundred dirhams."
"10157","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave every one of his wives a dower of twelve uqiyyas and a nashsh, and a nashsh is half an uqiyya; that is five hundred dirhams."
"10158","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Mujahid, who said: An uqiyya is forty dirhams, a nashsh is twenty, and a nawah is five dirhams."
"10159","From al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, who said: Abu Hadrad al-Aslami narrated to me that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking a ruling about a woman, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How much have you given her as dower? He said: Two hundred dirhams. He said: Had you been scooping it from But-han, you would not have given more."
"10160","From Ma'mar, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf with a trace of khaluq perfume on him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is this, Abd al-Rahman? He said: I have married a woman of the Ansar. He said: How much did you give her as dower? He said: The weight of a date-pit of gold. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Give a wedding feast, even if with a sheep. Anas said: I saw him allot to each of his wives after his death one hundred thousand."
"10161","From al-Thawri, from Humayd al-Tawil, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came to Madinah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between him and Sa'd ibn al-Rabi' al-Ansari. Sa'd offered to share with him his family and wealth, and he had two wives, but Abd al-Rahman said to him: May Allah bless your family and wealth for you; show me the market. He said: He went to the market and earned some dried cheese and some ghee. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him after some days with a trace of yellow on him and said: What is this, Abd al-Rahman? He said: I have married a woman of the Ansar. He said: What did you give her? He said: The weight of a date-pit of gold. He said: Give a wedding feast, even if with a sheep. Abd al-Razzaq said: Isma'il ibn Abd Allah reported to us from Humayd, from Anas: and that was two daniqs of gold."
"10162","From Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar, who said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best marriage is the easiest of it."
"10163","From al-Thawri, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: There is no harm in a man marrying even for a whip."
"10164","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ayyub, from Yazid ibn Qusayt, who said: I heard Ibn al-Musayyab say: Had he given her even a whip as dower, she would be lawful to him."
"10165","From al-Thawri, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: A man may marry even for a siwak stick of arak wood."
"10166","From Hasan, from a companion of his, from Sharik, who said: Dawud al-Za'farani reported to me from al-Sha'bi, from Ali, who said: The dower should not be less than ten dirhams."
"10167","He said: And Mughirah reported to me from Ibrahim, who said: I dislike the dower being like the wage of a prostitute; rather ten dirhams or twenty."
"10168","Ja'far reported from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, who said: Abu Talhah proposed to Umm Sulaym before he became Muslim, and she said: I am indeed inclined toward you, and one like you is not rejected, but you are a disbelieving man while I am a Muslim woman; if you become Muslim, that will be my dower, and I shall ask you for nothing else. So Abu Talhah became Muslim and married her."
"10169","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibrahim ibn Maysarah reported to me that his maternal aunt reported to him, from a trustworthy woman, who said: While my father was on a campaign in the pre-Islamic period, they became thirsty, and a man said: Who will give me his sandals, and I shall marry him to the first daughter born to me? My father removed his sandals and threw them to him. A girl was born to him and she grew up, and he said to him: Gather my family to me. He said: Bring the dower. He said: By Allah, I shall give you nothing more than what I gave you, the two sandals. He said: By Allah, I shall not bring her to you except for a dower. She said: My father went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of what is better than that? Leave her, so neither you nor your companion breaks an oath. So my father left her. He said: I thought he was one-eyed. She said: He carried me on the side of his blind eye until he brought me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10170","From Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he used to marry off his daughters for a thousand dinars or five hundred."
"10171","From Qays ibn al-Rabi', from Abu Husayn, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Do not be excessive in the dowries of women. A woman said: That is not for you, O Umar; Allah says: Even if you have given one of them a qintar of gold. He said: And likewise it is in the reading of Abd Allah: It is not lawful for you to take anything from it. Then Umar said: A woman disputed with Umar and overcame him in argument."
"10172","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: It was narrated to me from Ibn Umar that he said: A group went out on a campaign in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man said: Who will slaughter this sheep, and to him belongs my first daughter of my loins? A man slaughtered it, and a girl was born to him. They disputed before Ibn Mas'ud, and he awarded her to him and assigned her a dower like that of one of her womenfolk."
"10173","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: A man marries a woman and sends nothing to her, neither dower nor an appointed portion; what of her is lawful to him? He said: He should not touch her until he sends her a dower or an appointed portion. And Ibn al-Musayyab and Amr. I said to Ata: May he kiss her? I said: He should not touch her. He said: I do not mind his kissing her."
"10174","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: He named a dower for her but did not send it nor anything else. He said: That suffices; he may have intercourse with her if he wishes. I said: He sent her a gift for herself, not as part of the dower. He said: That suffices; he may have intercourse with her."
"10175","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata said: Anything he sends her or her family as a gift, other than the dower, without naming her dower, suffices, and it makes her lawful to him. And Amr."
"10176","From al-Thawri, from Mansur and Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that he saw no harm in a man marrying a woman and then consummating with her without paying anything in advance. Ibrahim said: That is more pleasing to me than a man giving part of the dower while intending to deceive regarding the rest. Sufyan said: He is like a man who buys a slave-girl and then has intercourse with her without paying."
"10177","From Mughirah, from Ibrahim, who said: When you have named the dower, there is no harm in your consummating with her, even if you have not paid anything in advance."
"10178","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, about a man who marries a woman and names a dower for her: is it permissible for him to go in to her without giving her anything? He said: Allah says: There is no blame upon you regarding what you mutually agree upon after the appointment. So when the dower has been appointed, there is no blame upon him in going in to her, though the established practice is that he present her something of clothing or maintenance."
"10179","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Talhah, from Khaythamah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married a woman and then sent her to her husband without giving her anything."
"10180","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: Do not consummate with your wife until you present something. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have nothing. He said: Give her your Hutamiyyah armor."
"10181","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub or another, from Ibn Sirin, that Ibn Abbas married a woman and went in to her without having presented anything before that, and he threw over her a cloak he was wearing."
"10182","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abu al-Zubayr reported to me that he heard Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, say: Ibn Abbas said: When a man marries a woman and names a dower for her, and wishes to go in to her, let him throw to her a cloak or a ring if he has one."
"10183","Ibn Jurayj reported, who said: Abu al-Zubayr reported to me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar."
"10184","From Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no shighar in Islam."
"10185","From Ma'mar, from Thabit and Aban, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no shighar in Islam, and shighar is for a man to exchange his sister for another man's sister without dower; and there is no is'ad in Islam, no jalab in Islam, and no janab."
"10186","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no shighar in Islam."
"10187","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: There is no shighar in Islam. Ma'mar said: I know it only from Anas."
"10188","From one who heard Anas say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no shighar, no is'ad in Islam, no confederate oath in Islam, no jalab, and no janab."
"10189","From Ma'mar, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: Shighar is for a man to exchange his sister for another man's sister without dower."
"10190","Ibn Jurayj reported from Ata, who said: Shighar is for one to marry this one to that one, and that one to this one, without dower except that."
"10191","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata was asked about a man where each of two men married the other his sister, with each preparing a small trousseau, though he could have taken more for her. He said: No; shighar was forbidden. I said: They have both given dowers. He said: No; each of them reduced it for his companion for his own sake."
"10192","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: One marries his virgin daughter for a dower, and both reduce it for the other for his own sake. He said: If they name a dower, there is no harm; but if one says: I shall prepare and you prepare, then no; that is shighar. I said: If this one leaves it unspecified and that one leaves it unspecified. He said: No."
"10193","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Hasan ibn Muslim reported to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam. As for jalab: a horse urged from behind by another horse; as for janab: one draws a horse alongside his horse so it runs faster thereby, and that is in racing."
"10194","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad and Ibn Jurayj, from Zayd ibn Aslam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man who marries a woman for a dower while having no intention in himself to pay it to her except that he will be with Allah a fornicator; and there is no man who buys a purchase from a man while having no intention to pay him except that he will be with Allah a traitor."
"10195","From Dawud ibn Ibrahim, who said: I heard Tawus say: The dower is the easiest of debts."
"10196","From Ja'far ibn Sulayman, who said: Amr ibn Dinar al-Ansari reported to me, who said: Some of the children of Suhayb narrated to me, who said: His sons asked him, saying: Why do you not narrate to us as the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrate? He said: I heard as they heard, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever deliberately lies about me will be burdened with tying a grain of barley in a knot, or else he will be punished."
"10197","But I shall narrate to you a hadith my hearing retained and my heart understood; I heard him say: Whoever marries a woman with the intention of depriving her of her right is a fornicator until he repents; and whoever bargains with a man in a sale with the intention of depriving him of his right is a traitor until he repents."
"10198","From Hisham, from al-Hasan, who said: When a man marries a woman and attests for her secretly twenty, and attests for her publicly thirty, he said: Her dower is the latter."
"10199","From al-Thawri, from Jabir and others, from al-Sha'bi, who said: When one marries secretly for a dower and publicly for a greater dower, the dower is what he named publicly. Sufyan said: Except when evidence establishes that he only made it heard, publicizing it falsely or for show."
"10200","From Ibn Jurayj and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a gathering in the mosque and said: What is this? They said: A marriage. He said: This is marriage, not fornication."
"10201","From Ma'mar and al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said regarding the sermon of need: Praise belongs to Allah; I seek His help and His forgiveness, and I seek refuge with Allah from the evils of ourselves. Whomever Allah guides, none can misguide, and whomever He misguides, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. And fear Allah through whom you ask one another, and the wombs. And do not die except as Muslims. Fear Allah and speak upright words, up to: And whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has attained a great triumph, Surah al-Ahzab verses 70-71. Then speak of your need."
"10202","From Hushaym ibn Bashir, who said: Mughirah narrated to me from Ibrahim, who said: They liked to pronounce the sermon when a man proposed for himself or for another, and when two litigants disputed: Praise belongs to Allah; we seek His help and His forgiveness, and we seek refuge with Allah from the evils of ourselves. Whomever Allah guides, none can misguide, and whomever He misguides, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Then it suffices a man to convey his need. He said: As for the two litigants, they state their needs."
"10203","From al-Thawri, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, who said: Husayn ibn Ali would marry some of the daughters of al-Hasan while he was gnawing a bone."
"10204","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Habib, freedman of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: Urwah sent me to Abd Allah ibn Umar to propose the daughter of Abd Allah for him. Abd Allah said: Yes; Urwah is indeed worthy of being married. Then he said: Call him. So I called him, and he did not leave until he married him. Habib said: None witnessed that but I, Urwah, and Abd Allah; but they announced it afterward and informed the people."
"10205","From al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Sulayman ibn Abi Yahya, who said: I proposed to Ibn Umar for one of his freedwomen, and he did no more than say: I marry you on condition that you retain in kindness or release with excellence."
"10206","Ibn Uyaynah reported from Bayan, who said: Bilal went to propose to a woman, with his brother with him. When they reached them, he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: I am Bilal and this is my brother; we are two men of Abyssinia; we were astray and Allah guided us, and we were slaves and Allah freed us. If you marry us, praise belongs to Allah; if you refuse us, glory belongs to Allah."
"10207","From Ma'mar, who said: A man of the Ansar narrated to me, raising the hadith, who said: Every momentous speech not begun with the remembrance of Allah is cut off."
"10208","From al-Thawri, who said: Abu Sa'id al-Basri narrated to me that he heard al-Hasan, and Ibn Jurayj reported to us from a man, from al-Hasan, mentioning from Aqil ibn Abi Talib: that he married a woman of Banu Jusham, and it was said to him: With comfort and sons. He said: Do not say that, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that and commanded us to say: May Allah bless for you and bless upon you."
"10209","From al-Thawri, from al-Ash'ath, from Adi ibn Artah, who said: I came to Shurayh and said to him: I have married a woman. He said: With comfort and sons."
"10210","From al-Thawri, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Abd Allah ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me in Shawwal, and I was brought to him in Shawwal. Which of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more fortunate with him than I? And she liked to bring her womenfolk in during Shawwal."
"10211","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, who said: A man of Bajilah came to Abd Allah and said: I have married a virgin girl, and I fear she may dislike me. Abd Allah said: Affection is from Allah, and aversion is from Satan, to make hateful to him what Allah has made lawful for him. When she is brought to you, command her to pray two rak'ahs behind you. Al-A'mash said: I mentioned it to Ibrahim, and he said: Abd Allah said: And say: O Allah, bless for me my family and bless for them in me; O Allah, provide me from them and provide them from me; O Allah, join us together as long as You join toward good, and separate us when You separate toward good."
"10212","From Ma'mar, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, who said: A man came to Ibn Mas'ud and said: I have married a woman, and I fear she may dislike me. Abd Allah said: Affection is from Allah, and aversion is from Satan, to make hateful to him what Allah has made lawful. When she is brought to you, command her to pray two rak'ahs behind you. Al-A'mash said: I mentioned it to Ibrahim. He said: And Abd Allah said: And say: O Allah, bless for me my family and bless for them in me; provide me from them and provide them from me; O Allah, join us together as long as You join toward good, and separate us when You separate toward good."
"10213","From al-Thawri, from Isma'il ibn Abd Allah, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Usayd, who said: I married a woman while I was a slave, and I invited the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among them Abu Dharr, Ibn Mas'ud, and Hudhayfah. Hudhayfah stepped forward to lead them in prayer, but Abu Dharr, or a man, said: That is not for you. So they put me forward while I was a slave, and I led them. They taught me, saying: When your wife is brought to you, pray two rak'ahs, command her to pray behind you, take hold of her forelock, ask Allah for good, and seek refuge with Allah from her evil."
"10214","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: It was narrated to me that Salman al-Farisi married a woman, and when he went in to her he stood at her door and found the house furnished level. He said: I do not know whether your house has a fever, or the Ka'bah has moved to Kindah? By Allah, I shall not enter it until its curtains are torn down. When they tore them down and nothing remained of them, he entered and saw much luggage and slave-girls. He said: What is this luggage? They said: Your wife's luggage and her slave-girls. He said: By Allah, my beloved did not command me with this; he commanded me to keep like the provision of a traveler. And he said to me: Whoever keeps of slave-girls more than he marries or gives in marriage, then they commit immorality, their sin is upon him. Then he went to his wife, placed his hand on her head, and said to those with her: Withdraw. None remained but his wife, and he said: Will you obey me, may Allah have mercy on you? She said: You have sat in the seat of one who is obeyed. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you marry one day, let the first thing you meet upon be obedience to Allah; so stand and let us pray two rak'ahs; whatever you hear me supplicate with, say amen."
"10215","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Al-Hasan said: It is enjoined that when a woman is brought to her husband in his house, he take hold of her forelock and supplicate for blessing."
"10216","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had one of them, when he comes to his wife—Mansur said: I think he said: In the name of Allah; O Allah, keep Satan away from us and keep Satan away from what You provide us—and a child is born between them, Satan will never harm him."
"10217","Ma'mar reported from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had one of them, when he has intercourse, said: O Allah, keep Satan away from us and keep Satan away from what You have provided us—and a child is decreed between them—Satan will not harm him, if Allah wills."
"10218","From Ja'far ibn Sulayman, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, who said: It is said: When a man comes to his wife, let him say: In the name of Allah; O Allah, bless for us what You have provided us, and grant Satan no share in what You have provided us. He said: It was hoped, if she conceived or received, that it would be a righteous child."
"10219","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: It was narrated to me from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man covers his wife, let him be truthful to her; if he fulfills his need while she has not fulfilled hers, let him not hurry her."
"10220","From al-Thawri, from Asim, from Abu Qilabah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to his wife, let him cover himself, and let them not strip as two donkeys strip."
"10221","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to his wife, let him cover himself, and let them not strip as two donkeys strip."
"10222","From Yahya ibn al-Ala, from Ibn An'um, that Sa'd ibn Mas'ud al-Kindi said: Uthman ibn Maz'un came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am shy that my wife should see my private part. He said: Allah has made you a garment for them and made them a garment for you. He said: I dislike that. He said: They see it of me, and I see it of them. He said: You, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I. He said: You; then who after you? He said: When Uthman turned away, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ibn Maz'un is indeed modest and concealing."
"10223","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Sulayman ibn Musa reported to me that Ibn Shihab reported to him that Urwah ibn al-Zubayr reported to him that Aishah reported to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who marries without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is void, her marriage is void; she has her dower for what he took of her. If they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian. I mentioned it to Ma'mar, and he said: I asked al-Zuhri about a man who marries without a guardian. He said: If he is a suitable match, they are not separated."
"10224","From Abd Allah ibn Muharrar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian and two just witnesses."
"10225","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, about a man who proposed to a woman to her guardian and married her with the testimony of a man and two women. He said: If they announce that, we consider it a permissible marriage, when they publicize it and do not conceal it."
"10226","From al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"10227","From Qays ibn al-Rabi', from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr, from Ali, who said: There is no marriage except with a guardian who permits."
"10228","From Abu Shaybah, from Abu Qays al-Awdi, that Ali used to say: When one marries without the permission of a guardian and then consummates with her, they are not separated; if he has not touched her, they are separated. From Ma'mar, from a man of Kufah, from Ali the like of it."
"10229","From al-Thawri, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl, that a woman was married off by her mother and maternal uncle, and Ali upheld her marriage."
"10230","From al-Thawri, from Isma'il al-Asadi, from al-Sha'bi, that he said: When he is a suitable match, the marriage is valid."
"10231","From Hushaym, from al-Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, that Umar, Ali, Ibn Mas'ud, and Shurayh did not validate marriage except with a guardian."
"10232","From Abd Allah ibn Muharrar, from Maymun ibn Mihran, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: Loose women are those who marry without a guardian; I think he said: There must be four: a suitor, a guardian, and two witnesses. From al-Thawri, from Abu Yahya, from a man, from Ibn Abbas the like of it."
"10233","From al-Thawri, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no marriage except with the permission of a guardian or a ruler."
"10234","Ibn Jurayj reported from Amr ibn Dinar, who said: The daughter of Abu Umamah, a woman of Banu Bakr of Kinanah ibn Mudarris, married. Alqamah ibn Abi Alqamah al-Utawari wrote to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz when he was in Madinah: I am her guardian, and she was married without my permission. Umar annulled it, though the man had already touched her."
"10235","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'bad, that Umar ibn al-Khattab annulled the marriage of a woman who married without the permission of her guardian."
"10236","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jubayr reported to me from Ikrimah ibn Khalid that the road gathered a caravan, and a previously married woman placed her affair with a man of the group other than a guardian, and he married her to a man. That reached Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he flogged the one who married and the one who gave in marriage, and annulled her marriage."
"10237","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: A woman married a man without the permission of the guardians while they were present, and he consummated with her. He said: And did she have witnesses? He said: Yes. He said: Any woman in charge of her affair, when there are witnesses, it is valid without the guardians; though had the guardian married her off, it would be more beloved to me, and her marriage is valid."
"10238","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, about a woman with no guardian who entrusted a man with her affair and he married her off. He said: Ibn Sirin used to say: There is no harm in it; the believers are guardians of one another. And al-Hasan used to say: They are separated, even if he touched her; if she has no guardian, then the ruler."
"10239","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, who said: I said to him: A man married with the testimony of women. He said: They are separated; if it is discovered, there is punishment, the least of which is said: A suitor and two witnesses."
"10240","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, who said: The difference between marriage and fornication is witnesses."
"10241","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, who said: The daughter of Husayn married Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf without the permission of her guardian; she married herself off. Hisham ibn Isma'il wrote to Abd al-Malik, and he wrote: Separate them; if he has gone in to her, she has her dower for what he made lawful of her, and if he has not gone in to her, he proposes to her along with the suitors."
"10242","From al-Thawri, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, who said: Women have nothing of the contract; he said: There is no marriage except with a guardian. From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah the like of it."
"10243","From Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A woman should not marry herself off, for the adulteress is the one who marries herself off."
"10244","From Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', who said: Umar entrusted his daughter Hafsah with his property and the marriage of his daughters; when Hafsah wished to marry off a woman, she would command her brother Abd Allah, and he would marry her off."
"10245","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that he used to say: A woman should not undertake the knot of marriage."
"10246","From Ma'mar, who said: One who heard Ikrimah reported to me, saying: When a woman wishes to marry off her slave-girl, she sends to her guardian and he marries her off."
"10247","From al-Thawri, who said: Ibn Umar was asked about a woman who owns a slave-girl: may she marry her off? He said: No; rather let her command her guardian to marry her off."
"10248","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: When Aishah wished to marry off a woman of her womenfolk, she would invite a group of her family and pronounce the sermon, until nothing remained but the marriage, and she would say: O so-and-so, marry; for women do not marry off."
"10249","From Muhammad ibn Rashid, who said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq and Abu Ma'shar reported to me that Ali called his wife Umamah, daughter of Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi', while he was ill, and spoke to her secretly; they think he said to her: Mu'awiyah will propose to you; if you wish to marry, then take a man of the household, pointing to me. When the people gathered to Mu'awiyah, he appointed Marwan over Madinah and said: Marry the Commander of the Believers to Umamah bint Abi al-As. That reached her, so she called al-Mughirah ibn Nawfal ibn al-Harith, entrusted him with her affair, and attested for him; he married her to himself and attested. Marwan became angry and stopped her, and wrote to Mu'awiyah informing him of that. He wrote to him: Leave him and her. Abd al-Razzaq said: Ali married her after the death of Fatimah."
"10250","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: A woman whom her paternal cousin proposes to, and she has no other man besides him. He said: Let her attest that so-and-so proposed to her, and I call you to witness that I have married him; otherwise let her command a man of her clan."
"10251","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, who said: Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah wished to marry a woman to whom he was closer than the one he wanted to marry her off to, so he commanded another more distant than him, and he married her to him. Sufyan said: An umm walad is of that standing: when he frees her and then wishes to marry her."
"10252","From al-Thawri, who said: He was asked about three brothers, one of whom married off his sister while the other two denied. He said: When he is a suitable match, the marriage is valid."
"10253","From al-Thawri, who said: We heard that the private part is to the paternal relatives, and property to the executors, from one deemed trustworthy."
"10254","From al-Thawri, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, who said: Ziyad said: Any woman who inclines to a man, we look; if we see she inclines to a suitable match, we marry her off even if the guardian refuses; if she inclines to an unsuitable one, we do not marry her off. Sufyan said: If the ruler or guardian says: He is suitable, but she refuses, she is not compelled to him."
"10255","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, who said: I asked al-Hasan, saying: A weak woman among us with no one; may she entrust a man who marries her off? He said: There is no marriage except with a guardian. He said: I kept debating it with him and minimizing her matter to him, and he said: She has no marriage except with the permission of her guardian. He said: When I pressed him much, he said: By Allah, I know nothing but that. He said: I said: And the judge? He said: And the judge."
"10256","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, asked about a woman who married herself to a man, paid the dower on his behalf, and stipulated that separation and intercourse be in her hand. He said: This is rejected, and it is a marriage not lawful."
"10257","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, that Ibn Abbas ruled about a woman who married herself to a man, paid him the dower, and stipulated that intercourse and separation be in her hand: he awarded her against him the dower, and that intercourse and separation be in his hand."
"10258","From Ma'mar, who said: I asked Hammad about a man found with a woman; she said: My husband, and the man said: My wife. It was said: Where are the witnesses? They said: They died or are absent. The hadd is averted from them. Ma'mar said: And Qatadah said: The hadd is carried out upon them when they confess."
"10259","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, who said: Whoever marries not in the manner of marriage and then divorces, it counts as nothing; he only divorced one not his wife."
"10260","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, who said: Every marriage in the manner of marriage, when there is separation in it, even if not mentioned, the marriage was not upon the sunnah practice, it is one; if it was not in the manner of marriage, then nothing."
"10261","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, who said: Every separation occurring in a marriage whose form was upon the sunnah, that separation is a divorce; if it was upon the sunnah practice and they separated, it is not divorce."
"10262","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, who said: Every marriage not in the manner of marriage, if he divorces, his divorce is nothing."
"10263","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: A man married a woman without witnesses and consummated with her. He said: The least done with them is that they be flogged the lesser hadd, then separated; she observes waiting, then I do not know—perhaps I shall not let him marry her until he attests two just witnesses as Allah said. Ibn Jurayj said it, and Abd al-Karim said it."
"10264","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I asked Ata about a man who married a woman and she turned out to be his sister through nursing: is it ihsan? He said: No. He said: Does that make her lawful to a husband if he had consummated with her? He said: No."
"10265","From al-Thawri, from Abu Sahl, from al-Sha'bi, about a man who marries his wife's sister. He said: She has her dower, he separates from her, he keeps away from his first wife until the waiting period of this one he separated from ends, and the dower of this latter is upon the one who deceived him."
"10266","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: It was reported to me from Ali that he said about a man who married a woman and touched her, then went to another land and married a woman and touched her, and she turned out to be her sister: he ruled that he separate from the latter and return to the former, except that he not touch the former until this one completes her waiting period."
"10267","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, who said: Had a man unknowingly married a sister of his through nursing, that would not be ihsan until he marries a marriage with no doubt in it."
"10268","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, who said: The marriage of her brother through nursing, unknowingly, does not make her lawful to a husband, even if he consummated, until she marries a marriage with no confusion in it."
"10269","From al-Thawri, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, about a man who marries a woman while she is his sister through nursing. He said: She has the dower for what he took of her."
"10270","From al-Thawri, about a man who married a woman and did not go in to her, then married a small nursing infant, whereupon the mother of his first wife nursed her. He said: Both become void; the dower is upon the mother who nursed—half the dower to each of them—because the corruption came from her. Then he marries whichever of them he wishes. If he had gone in to the first, she has the full dower upon him, and upon the mother half the dower for the small one. If he wishes, he marries her during her waiting period, because she is within a hundred, and that is not lawful for another; it is not a divorce but a separation. He may not marry the small one during the waiting period of the first."
"10271","From Ma'mar, who said: I asked Hammad about a man who married a woman and did not go in to her until he went to another land, married a woman and went in to her, and she turned out to be her sister through nursing. He said: He is separated from both of them entirely; she has her dower for what he made lawful. When the waiting period of the one he went in to passes, she marries him if she wishes."
"10272","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, about a man who married a woman then did not go in to her until he went to another land, married another woman and went in to her, and she turned out to be the mother of the one he married. He said: He is separated from both of them, and neither of them is ever lawful to him."
"10273","From al-Thawri, who said: When a man has intercourse with his wife's mother or his wife's daughter, both become void for him entirely."
"10274","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani, who said: A trustworthy one reported to me from Abd Allah ibn Ma'qil ibn Muqarrin that he said about a man who marries a woman and goes in to her, then marries her mother in another land unknowingly and goes in to her: Both become forbidden to him entirely."
"10275","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, about a man who married a woman and had intercourse with her, then went to another land, married another woman and touched her, and she turned out to be her sister. They said: He is separated from the latter; she has her dower for what he took of her. Qatadah said: He keeps away from his first wife until the waiting period of this latter ends."
"10276","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, about a man who marries his sister through nursing unknowingly until she dies: He inherits her."
"10277","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, who said: There is no inheritance between them. And Ma'mar preferred the saying of al-Zuhri."
"10278","From al-Thawri, about two men in a gathering, one of whom said to the other: Marry me your sister, and I shall give you my slave so-and-so and so-and-so. He said: Yes. He said: Go to your sister and inform her. He went in to her and she disliked it, saying: Everything you take from him is free. Her brother went out and informed him of that. Then her brother said: That is not it; go and enter upon your wife. He went and entered upon her, while her brother sat at the door until he lay with her. Al-Thawri said: It was not a marriage; she has a like dower for what he took of her, they are separated, and if she wishes she marries him afterward."
"10279","From al-Thawri, about a man who married off his sister while she was absent; when it reached her she denied it. It was said to her: The man is wealthy, and he is a match for you. She said: I am pleased. He said: The marriage has lapsed; let them renew her marriage."
"10280","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, about a man and woman separated in a marriage they did not intend: a man married his sister through nursing unknowingly and touched her. He said: She does not have the whole dower; she has half of it."
"10281","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata reported to me that Ali ibn Abi Talib was brought a woman married in her waiting period and consummated with; he separated them and commanded her to observe what remained of her first waiting period, then observe a fresh waiting period from this one. When her waiting period ends, she has the choice: if she wishes she marries, and if she wishes not. And another besides Ata said to me in this hadith: She has her dower. And Ata said: She has her dower for what he took of her."
"10282","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: It was reported to me that Ibn Mas'ud said about her the saying of Ali: She marries him if she wishes when her waiting period ends, differing with Umar."
"10283","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, who said: Ali said: He marries her if he wishes when her waiting period ends, and she has her dower."
"10284","From Ma'mar, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, who said: She has her dower."
"10285","From al-Thawri, from Salih, from al-Sha'bi: If he wishes, he said: He marries her when her waiting period ends."
